{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up","id":978952,"title":"So the White Wolf Q&A from Grand Masquerade is up","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-30T05:04:06-07:00","id":978952,"title":"So the White Wolf Q&A from Grand Masquerade is up","content":"Right here: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8fhpXrrLBsI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8fhpXrrLBsI</a><br /> <br /> About 20 minutes in, there's a question about the old vs. new World of Darkness. Shane DeFreest makes a comment to the effect that the World of Darkness was designed as a world first and then a game, but that the Chronicles of Darkness was designed as a game first, and that this is a flaw. I'm not sure what to think wrt that, given that I generally like ChroD versions of games more than CWoD versions. Martin Ericsson's response is a bit kinder to ChroD.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to pick an argument or anything here, but I am wondering what people think about the commentary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:19:28-07:00","id":978974,"title":"","content":"Honestly I've seen nothing but tasteless remarks re: ChroD from them since the acquisition.<br /> <br /> I'm just super grateful they've let OPP continue to do their thing, because if they hadn't, I'd have had to find a new hobby. Games in the style of CWoD are completely and totally unenjoyable to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:28:35-07:00","id":978976,"title":"","content":"*Facedesk*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:32:56-07:00","id":978980,"title":"","content":"It struck me as a bit... off... that Shane would make comments about Onyx Path's work like that.<br /> <br /> I don't really see ChroD as being &quot;game first, then setting&quot; in the way Shane said it was. I mean clearly it was developed and evolved differently from the CWoD in a lot of ways, many of which involved applying lessons learned when CWoD was the thing. I don't think they were perfect as such - I'm glad ChroD games are getting a second edition, and for example I much prefer Vampire's second edition to first edition.<br /> <br /> But all that aside, I've never really tried to compare the two very explicitly, beyond the fact that I just like Vampire and Werewolf better in ChroD than CWoD (I still need to read Mage and Changeling). Why I like them better is due to thematic matters and the kind of emotional mood they evoke in both the core books and the supplements. And there's not really any &quot;metaplot,&quot; which I got tired of by the time CWoD had hit Gehenna/Apocalypse/Ascension/etc. I still have a lot of nostalgic love for these games, and would still run (I am thinking of a CWoD V20 Vampire game right now) and play them, I am more inclined to turn to ChroD in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:18:46-07:00","id":979000,"title":"","content":"Fair warning, unpopular opinion follows.<br /> <br /> The Q&amp;A provided an interesting insight into why US politics is such a messed up place to dwell in or ponder about. They talked about all those great things they want to show in their games, how corporate corruption and control of politics has poisoned our society and environment, how politics is a rigged game, how class war is still a thing, how racism and sexism is an abomination perpetuated by the need to keep the herd separated (in a sort of branching out way, the system has even its own victims attacking other victims of the system).<br /> <br /> As an active leftist, I don't want to perpetuate the false sense that the world is heading some place pleasant. I lived through the capitalist exploitation of several countries to know better. As a vegan, I don't want to hide away the ugly truths of the meat industry, I wanna play a werewolf that rips apart a Pentex executive for fucking with Gaia. As a feminist, I want to see the face of that smug Tremere sexist, when he realizes my female character is about to diablerize his sorry ass.<br /> <br /> The audience kept repeating the same mantras about gender politics and white privilege. I am not white (at least not of European or North American descent anyway). It was uncomfortable because I now kinda get why someone would be satisfied with Clinton running for the presidency, despite being a warmongering, corporate sell out and threat to the globe. I already knew the amount of ignorance it takes to support Trump (a lying psychopath). It really pains me because of what could've been, a kind of generalized struggle against the monster and its many heads (in the event of a Bernie Sanders nomination by the Dems).<br /> <br /> And I'm fucking glad WW wants to bring Punk back. I don't want to feel safe in the system, I want to see it go fuck itself.<br /> <br /> Edit: In case anyone's wondering, I would be voting for Stein if I were a US citizen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 09-30-2016, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:25:05-07:00","id":979004,"title":"","content":"Can't watch Youtube atm, can you provide us with direct quotes? From both Shane and Ericsson?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:03:49-07:00","id":979024,"title":"","content":"I'm going to assume the best of his statement, and there is some truth to it.<br /> <br /> The WoD, for better and worse, was all about the world building. The further it went along, the more it became about the things in the world and how characters interact with that canon than it was about establishing mood or creating a vehicle for GMs and players to build their own worlds. Who do your characters side with in the Camarilla/Sabbat war? How do they interact with vampire Al Capone? Will they meet Caine? It became more and more prevalent as the game advanced and metaplot tended to take center stage. The story moved forward as basically an editorial-level chronicle, and characters figured out how they fit into the cogs of that grand scope. The tagline was always &quot;This is our world, but darker&quot;, but the further and further the game went on, the less and less that was true. It was more &quot;This is a high urban fantasy setting that kind of-sort of looks like our world&quot;. (There's nothing wrong with that, of course, and I have a lot of love for the earnest and sometimes goofy aspects of the world).<br /> <br /> ChroD is more of a toolkit. It gives you themes and moods and mechanics that accommodate those. It provides template organizations and lets you figure out how those interact with each other. The four organizations in Requiem, for instance, can be mixed and matched innumerable ways to create distinct settings for any city. Focusing on the city/regional level makes it a setting-neutral game, which I actually find very refreshing. There's no long, tangled canon history describing the origins of vampirism or the history of the War of Rage. There's just myths and shaky historiography that might or might not be true. Even the blue books are designed in a more modular way. Look at Precinct 13 or Damnation City. They have sample templates in there, but they're designed to be modular rather than world-building supplements. I think it basically is a game-first thing, but I don't think that's a bad thing at all. In fact, I prefer it.<br /> <br /> I'm giving the dude benefit of the doubt and assuming that was his intent.<br /> <br /> Edit: Never mind. Just read it. They're very wrong, and those comments were insulting. I love the cWoD, but it's silly to hear them talking about it with such pretensions. I mean, I was glad that they tried to be progressive with their books, but in retrospective, a lot of their attempts at being forward thinking were silly and shallow and posturing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-30-2016, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:22:39-07:00","id":979035,"title":"","content":"It's the Grand Masquerade, celebrating the 25th Anniversary of old World of Darkness. I'm surprised anyone even brought up Chronicles, but I wouldn't be surprised at all if it was in a negative light. As it is it sounds like someone who doesn't have much experience with Chronicles, based solely on Resplendent Fire's post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:26:17-07:00","id":979038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979035#post979035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the Grand Masquerade, celebrating the 25th Anniversary of old World of Darkness. I'm surprised anyone even brought up Chronicles, but I wouldn't be surprised at all if it was in a negative light. As it is it sounds like someone who doesn't have much experience with Chronicles, based solely on Resplendent Fire's post.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I know, weirdly, there <i>still</i> seems to be a lot of factionalism about &quot;which is better&quot;. I see it in players in my city, where that whole &quot;my game is better than your game&quot; stance is pretty militant and aggressive, on both sides of the fence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:28:49-07:00","id":979043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979038#post979038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I know, weirdly, there <i>still</i> seems to be a lot of factionalism about &quot;which is better&quot;. I see it in players in my city, where that whole &quot;my game is better than your game&quot; stance is pretty militant and aggressive, on both sides of the fence.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there's other reasons, there's people on both sides who believe that their side isn't getting enough attention due to the other. Not just in terms of books, but if everyone in town is playing the other game, it's going to be harder to get people to come play yours.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:33:06-07:00","id":979050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979043#post979043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While there's other reasons, there's people on both sides who believe that their side isn't getting enough attention due to the other. Not just in terms of books, but if everyone in town is playing the other game, it's going to be harder to get people to come play yours.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, there's absolutely a level of that. I know my group (who skew a bit younger) look at the cWoD as very &quot;edgelord&quot;: lots of trenchcoats and katanas and gold-plated desert eagles, but the majority of gamers in town are staunchly cWoD.<br /> <br /> I grew up with the cWoD and still have a lot of fondness for it, but I think a lot of that is nostalgia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:43:19-07:00","id":979063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979050#post979050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh yeah, there's absolutely a level of that. I know my group (who skew a bit younger) look at the cWoD as very &quot;edgelord&quot;: lots of trenchcoats and katanas and gold-plated desert eagles, but the majority of gamers in town are staunchly cWoD.<br /> <br /> I grew up with the cWoD and still have a lot of fondness for it, but I think a lot of that is nostalgia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of it might just be simple human factionalism - what I like is better, and anything other must be worse. But game systems can each have their strengths. They're only better or worse when meeting specific tastes or tasks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:45:49-07:00","id":979066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979063#post979063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of it might just be simple human factionalism - what I like is better, and anything other must be worse. But game systems can each have their strengths. They're only better or worse when meeting specific tastes or tasks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. ChroD is basically what I want at this point in my life, but I understand the appeal of CoD too. I'll probably pick up the fifth edition. I doubt I'll get the chance to play it, but it will be a nice bit of nostalgia at the least.<br /> <br /> And there's most definitely a bit of just factionalism. See DC vs. Marvel and console wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:51:01-07:00","id":979074,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think White Wolf is just trying to score points with cWoD fans by down-talking ChroD. They kind of have been since the beginning. The very &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; pitch reads like something trying to win over people who resented the split between classic and new. Re-naming nWoD made sense, but it's also a gesture that says &quot;this isn't the <i>real</i> World of Darkness.&quot; Martin's comments in that one interview about how &quot;the fans&quot; hated nWoD were very telling as to what fans they are interested in catering to. And this &quot;WoD is a world first and a game second, ChroD is a game first and a world second&quot; thing sounds like something only a person who knows nothing about ChroD and is just going by what they've heard from people who skimmed the original Requiem, Forsaken, and Awakening core books would say. Which I'm pretty sure is not true of Shane, which leads me to suspect he's just saying it to win over cWoD fans who that is true of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":".  Fixing typos 09-30-2016, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:54:06-07:00","id":979078,"title":"","content":"'Lets make World of Darkness great again.'<br /> <br /> Still, if it gets people excited about the game, good for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:02:32-07:00","id":979085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979074#post979074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think White Wolf is just trying to score points with cWoD fans by down-talking ChroD. They kind of have been since the beginning. The very &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; pitch reads like something trying to win over people who resented the split between classic and new. Re-naming nWoD made sense, but it's also a gesture that says &quot;this isn't the <i>real</i> World of Darkness. Martin's comments in that one interview about how &quot;the fans hated&quot; nWoD were very telling as to what fans they are interested in catering to. And this &quot;WoD is a world first and a game second, ChroD is a game first and a world second&quot; sounds like something only a person who knows nothing about ChroD and is just going by what they've heard from people who skimmed the original Requiem, Forsaken, and Awakening core books. Which I'm pretty sure is not true of Shane, which leads me to suspect he's just saying it to win over cWoD fans who that is true of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a more apt (and less aggressive) way of framing it would be to say that CoD is more about externalized struggle (hence the &quot;punk&quot; element), and ChroD is more about internalized struggle. CoD tends to be more players against the machine (whether that's the Camarilla, the Wyrm/Weaver, or the Technocracy). ChroD is more about how your characters hold onto their integrity in the face of challenges (keeping your sanity in the face of darkness as a mortal, using the people and things you love as an anchor for your humanity in Requiem, balancing your primal urges in Forsaken, learning what it is to be human in Prometheus).<br /> <br /> As long as we keep getting ChroD books, I'm entirely fine with the split and with Paradox hyping the core fanbase however they want. That said, I would have loved to see them say some positive things about lessons learned. ChroD does a very good job of marrying themes to mechanics and making the day-to-day lives of characters more important, and I'd like to see them reinterpret some of those strengths for the cWoD. Hell, the game lines have been around a decade now. You'd think there'd be some positive lessons there. But then again, I'm not the audience they're appealing to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-30-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:18:01-07:00","id":979093,"title":"","content":"I think his whole &quot;setting first&quot; comment is also in part about pushing the whole multimedia angle. They seem to be emphasizing an aggressive push towards expansion into video games, film, and TV, and having a series bible. In other words, they seem to want a more IP based model similar to what WotC is doing with D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> That of course means legitimizing this model and distancing themselves from ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:18:26-07:00","id":979095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979085#post979085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a more apt (and less aggressive) way of framing it would be to say that CoD is more about externalized struggle (hence the &amp;quot;punk&amp;quot; element), and ChroD is more about internalized struggle. CoD tends to be more players against the machine (whether that's the Camarilla, the Wyrm/Weaver, or the Technocracy). ChroD is more about how your characters hold onto their integrity in the face of challenges (keeping your sanity in the face of darkness as a mortal, using the people and things you love as an anchor for your humanity in Requiem, balancing your primal urges in Forsaken, learning what it is to be human in Prometheus).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. To sum it up in a soundbite-sized phrase, WoD is Punk, ChroD is Goth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979085#post979085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as we keep getting ChroD books, I'm entirely fine with the split and with Paradox hyping the core fanbase however they want. That said, I would have loved to see them say some positive things about lessons learned. ChroD does a very good job of marrying themes to mechanics and making the day-to-day lives of characters more important, and I'd like to see them reinterpret some of those strengths for the cWoD. Hell, the game lines have been around a decade now. You'd think there'd be some positive lessons there. But then again, I'm not the audience they're appealing to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, at this point I don't much care what White Wolf thinks of ChroD. As long as they're going to let Onyx Path continue to do their thing, I'll continue to enjoy it. It would be nice if they could comment on ChroD without oozing disdain, but whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:18:27-07:00","id":979096,"title":"","content":"Considering that I'm spending my money so I can <i>play a game</i> and not <i>read a novel</i>, the claim that nWoD is a game first while oWoD is a setting first falls flat as an insult to me. Maybe if oWoD had been put together with an eye a little more focused on the <i>game</i> aspect, the mechanics wouldn't look so much like a thirteen year old's first self-published rule set in places.<br /> <br /> People are allowed to like different things. It's just more than a little trashy to shit on the successor game line to the original game because it wasn't enough like the original game line for your tastes. <i>Especially</i> when essentially all you're doing is re-publishing the original game line and not making anything new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:21:47-07:00","id":979098,"title":"","content":"Do they mention anything about the release in 2016?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:28:30-07:00","id":979103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979093#post979093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think his whole &amp;quot;setting first&amp;quot; comment is also in part about pushing the whole multimedia angle. They seem to be emphasizing an aggressive push towards expansion into video games, film, and TV, and having a series bible. In other words, they seem to want a more IP based model similar to what WotC is doing with D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> That of course means legitimizing this model and distancing themselves from ChroD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. And to their credit, WoD is absolutely the better choice for a multimedia brand. The WoD metaplot lends itself to a setting bible in a way the ChroD toolbox never could, and the only way I could see a ChroD TV show working is as something like American Horror Story where each season is a self-contained story starring the same actors. But since American Horror Story already does that, it wouldn't be as marketable to a network. Like, everything they've been doing makes sense given their business plan, which is part of why I'm more inclined to believe that the consistent displays of negativity towards ChroD is calculated. If they actually disliked ChroD, they could have killed it (as Martin was so keen to point out), but they didn't. I doubt they have any beef with ChroD, they just know their target audience likes when they talk shit about it. Which is obnoxious, but as long as they leave ChroD alone otherwise, I can shrug off their distasteful comments about it and keep playing my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:31:05-07:00","id":979107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979103#post979103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, absolutely. And to their credit, WoD is absolutely the better choice for a multimedia brand. The WoD metaplot lends itself to a setting bible in a way the ChroD toolbox never could, and the only way I could see a ChroD TV show working is as something like American Horror Story where each season is a self-contained story starring the same actors. But since American Horror Story already does that, it wouldn't be as marketable to a network. Like, everything they've been doing makes sense given their business plan, which is part of why I'm more inclined to believe that the consistent displays of negativity towards ChroD is calculated. If they actually disliked ChroD, they could have killed it (as Martin was so keen to point out), but they didn't. I doubt they have any beef with ChroD, they just know their target audience likes when they talk shit about it. Which is obnoxious, but as long as they leave ChroD alone otherwise, I can shrug off their distasteful comments about it and keep playing my games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, agreed there. My only disappointment is that we won't be getting any ChroD video games. I think there's a lot of amazing potential there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:41:37-07:00","id":979114,"title":"","content":"With all the stuff that has come out about CoD and WoD from the new WW people, I am very glad the the new WW people have let OP continue what they've been doing with regards to the CoD, because I would hate to see this game fall on the wayside. That said, I am so bloody excited to see where they are taking the WoD with regards to VtM at least. All of this talk of advancing the metaplot and trying to make the games actually work together has me pulling out my wallet like its CoD 3e kickstarters already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:48:53-07:00","id":979119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979107#post979107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, agreed there. My only disappointment is that we won't be getting any ChroD video games. I think there's a lot of amazing potential there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a bummer. I was also disappointed by the lack of LARP support, but what else is new. Honestly though, if the WoD games they make are half as good as Bloodlines, I'll still enjoy the crap out of them and that should give me enough of a [blank] of Darkness video game fix to be satisfied. Heck, if there's good enough mod support, maybe we'll even see ChroD mods for WoD games. It'd be pretty doable in Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I'm also really hoping they succeed in getting a WoD Netflix series, mostly because I'm pretty sure I could get my parents hooked on that if it was halfway decent and that would just be hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:58:21-07:00","id":979125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979093#post979093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think his whole &amp;quot;setting first&amp;quot; comment is also in part about pushing the whole multimedia angle. They seem to be emphasizing an aggressive push towards expansion into video games, film, and TV, and having a series bible. In other words, they seem to want a more IP based model similar to what WotC is doing with D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> That of course means legitimizing this model and distancing themselves from ChroD.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly after seeing how the transmedia approach has royally fucked over the well designed 5e and starved the D&amp;D settings, I mean no FRCG even, I'm glad as a CoD fan, that White Wolf is focusing its transmedia crap on OWOD and leaving CoD alone.<br /> <br /> So they can diss CoD, no problem, because it means its beneath under White Wolfs corporate gaze, which means far, far greater creative freedom for the CoD.<br /> <br /> Some times its nice having less expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:51:50-07:00","id":979176,"title":"","content":"I don't think the idea that World of Darkness has a bigger cultural buy in is wrong, so I totally understand why it's the more effective transmedia vehicle. And while I sort of disagree with the idea that Chronicles of Darkness isn't a vehicle to talk about social issues, I thought Martin was fairly forthright and respectful, and supposedly he *loves* Promethean, so take that as you will.<br /> <br /> Shane's answer sure was a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:50:28-07:00","id":979214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979176#post979176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while I sort of disagree with the idea that Chronicles of Darkness isn't a vehicle to talk about social issues</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah, he said <i>what</i> now? I'm going to have to watch the video when I get home before I draw any conclusions, but between this and his comments about how WoD should be able to address 9/11 as a metaplot point... I'm pretty sure he and I have very different views on what &quot;talking about social issues&quot; should look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:12:07-07:00","id":979229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979119#post979119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a bummer. I was also disappointed by the lack of LARP support, but what else is new. Honestly though, if the WoD games they make are half as good as Bloodlines, I'll still enjoy the crap out of them and that should give me enough of a [blank] of Darkness video game fix to be satisfied. Heck, if there's good enough mod support, maybe we'll even see ChroD mods for WoD games. It'd be pretty doable in Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I'm also really hoping they succeed in getting a WoD Netflix series, mostly because I'm pretty sure I could get my parents hooked on that if it was halfway decent and that would just be hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I view this as a first step. If new WoD video games, LARP materials, and media series do well then the overall visibility and viability of the other WW/OP IPs goes up, increasing the odds of them also getting more attention in the future.<br /> <br /> I.E. we were never going to get Luke Cage without Iron Man happening first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:18:47-07:00","id":979231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979214#post979214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah, he said <i>what</i> now? I'm going to have to watch the video when I get home before I draw any conclusions, but between this and his comments about how WoD should be able to address 9/11 as a metaplot point... I'm pretty sure he and I have very different views on what &amp;quot;talking about social issues&amp;quot; should look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't put it like that, but that was sort of an unintended implication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:54:10-07:00","id":979248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979229#post979229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I view this as a first step. If new WoD video games, LARP materials, and media series do well then the overall visibility and viability of the other WW/OP IPs goes up, increasing the odds of them also getting more attention in the future.<br /> <br /> I.E. we were never going to get Luke Cage without Iron Man happening first.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an optimistic way of looking at it, and I would like to agree with you. But, I think they've made it pretty clear that they don't plan on doing that. It kind of goes against their One World of Darkness vision, even if it's called Chronicles now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:54:03-07:00","id":979301,"title":"","content":"Ok, now that I've had the chance to watch the video, I actually really appreciate Martin's answer. I definitely don't agree with all of his assessments of the two IPs, but he expressed his viewpoint and his reasoning eloquently, and respectfully. <br /> <br /> Re: WoD having made a meaningful impact on people's lives and identities in a way that ChroD hasn't to the same extent, this just speaks to a bias towards a particular generation of gamers. Maybe that's true for people who were in high school or college in the 90s, but us millennials weren't playing Masquerade in our formative years, we were playing Requiem. To be fair, tabletop gaming was bigger in the 90s, so there probably is some truth to the idea that WoD may have had that kind of impact on a greater number of people's lives. And that may have been what he meant when he added &quot;to the same extent&quot;.<br /> <br /> Re: the assertion that WoD was chosen as the IP White Wolf wanted to push because it was able to speak to real things going on in the here and now (or to be more accurate, that <i>were</i> going on in the here and now of 20 years ago) and the unspoken implication that WoD does not, this goes back to the &quot;WoD is Punk, ChroD is Goth&quot; thing. They are both very visceral responses to very real issues in the world. WoD just responds in an external, angry way, where ChroD responds in an internal, reflective way. Again, I think recognizing the impact of one and not the other just speaks to a generational bias.<br /> <br /> At any rate, It's clear he learned his lesson after the backlash from that interview I referred to earlier because this time he really seemed to take great care to explain himself without speaking negatively of ChroD. I also don't think he answered the question that was actually asked, but that's neither here nor there. The same cannot be said of Shane, who I think did try to answer the actual question, but did so without any regard for ChroD or ChroD fans, or even attempting to hide his disdain for ChroD. And it's not like it would have been hard to express that answer without insulting ChroD. He's not exactly <i>wrong</i> that ChroD makes tabletop gameplay a higher priority than WoD does, and that priority comes at the cost of other priorities. But the way he presents that props WoD up as a more believable world (which... huh?) and dismisses ChroD's quite extensive worldbuilding as &quot;layering other stuff on top of (the gameplay)&quot;. Also, the &quot;I hope that doesn't happen again&quot; bit at the end was unnecessary and a cheap shot. The &quot;how much time do you have?&quot; could have gone either way, but in the context of the rest of his answer was also an unnecessary dig at ChroD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-30-2016, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:08:27-07:00","id":979307,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Shane's response bothered me the most. If I'd been less annoyed this morning I would have transcribed.<br /> <br /> I also appreciate Martin's answer as more nuanced and accurate, and I agree that this is about a generational focus (on my generation, as it happens - I spent most of the 90s playing Vampire (LARP and tabletop), Werewolf (LARP), and Mage (tabletop), and I still love those games like few others. But I also hate to see ChroD get short shrift when it does so many things <i>better</i> than classic WoD did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:21:48-07:00","id":979315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979301#post979301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, now that I've had the chance to watch the video, I actually really appreciate Martin's answer. I definitely don't agree with all of his assessments of the two IPs, but he expressed his viewpoint and his reasoning eloquently, and respectfully.<br /> <br /> Re: WoD having made a meaningful impact on people's lives and identities in a way that ChroD hasn't to the same extent, this just speaks to a bias towards a particular generation of gamers. Maybe that's true for people who were in high school or college in the 90s, but us millennials weren't playing Masquerade in our formative years, we were playing Requiem. To be fair, tabletop gaming was bigger in the 90s, so there probably is some truth to the idea that WoD may have had that kind of impact on a greater number of people's lives. And that may have been what he meant when he added &quot;to the same extent&quot;.<br /> <br /> Re: the assertion that WoD was chosen as the IP White Wolf wanted to push because it was able to speak to real things going on in the here and now (or to be more accurate, that <i>were</i> going on in the here and now of 20 years ago) and the unspoken implication that WoD does not, this goes back to the &quot;WoD is Punk, ChroD is Goth&quot; thing. They are both very visceral responses to very real issues in the world. WoD just responds in an external, angry way, where ChroD responds in an internal, reflective way. Again, I think recognizing the impact of one and not the other just speaks to a generational bias.<br /> <br /> At any rate, It's clear he learned his lesson after the backlash from that interview I referred to earlier because this time he really seemed to take great care to explain himself without speaking negatively of ChroD. I also don't think he answered the question that was actually asked, but that's neither here nor there. The same cannot be said of Shane, who I think did try to answer the actual question, but did so without any regard for ChroD or ChroD fans, or even attempting to hide his disdain for ChroD. And it's not like it would have been hard to express that answer without insulting ChroD. He's not exactly <i>wrong</i> that ChroD makes tabletop gameplay a higher priority than WoD does, and that priority comes at the cost of other priorities. But the way he presents that props WoD up as a more believable world (which... huh?) and dismisses ChroD's quite extensive worldbuilding as &quot;layering other stuff on top of (the gameplay)&quot;. Also, the &quot;I hope that doesn't happen again&quot; bit at the end was unnecessary and a cheap shot. The &quot;how much time do you have?&quot; could have gone either way, but in the context of the rest of his answer was also an unnecessary dig at ChroD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it was mostly Shane's comment that irked me. And he's welcome to his opinion, of course, and if it were a different context, whatever, but it's kind of bad optics to have sour grapes over your own intellectual property. If that wasn't his intent, it sure came off that way.<br /> <br /> I do hearten that Dhaunae's involved, though. She's been on the <i>cover </i>of a CofD book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:29:08-07:00","id":979317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l-