animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the one. I like to think that every time she shows up in book art, she's just found a new Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Something about that picture's been bugging me since it came out. It's a great picture but I could never figure out what about it kept nagging me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:48:07-07:00","id":979518,"title":"","content":"Times like this, I'm glad that Chronicles isn't the chosen one\u2122.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T23:05:04-07:00","id":979527,"title":"","content":"Being perfectly honest, our Paradox overlords seem to be stuck in the past. Time will tell if that pays out or not, but even as a punk born too late, I've yet to hear anything from Paradox that inspires me to care. While I am vastly annoyed at the denial of opportunity for expanded ChroD media beyond the ttrpg's(even as I understand the need, from a business standpoint, to pick a horse and maybe come back to other things as it proves profitable), I'm just as vastly grateful that they're leaving it up to Onyx Path, that's how unimpressed I am with their marketing play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T00:15:36-07:00","id":979539,"title":"","content":"Well Arc, prepare to be even less impressed due to their answer to the 2nd question in this <a href=\"http://keepontheheathlands.com/2016/09/30/the-future-of-darkness-an-interview-with-white-wolf-publishing/\" target=\"_blank\">interview</a>. That's right, they're bring the unmentionable book back","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T00:33:02-07:00","id":979543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979539#post979539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Arc, prepare to be even less impressed due to their answer to the 2nd question in this <a href=\"http://keepontheheathlands.com/2016/09/30/the-future-of-darkness-an-interview-with-white-wolf-publishing/\" target=\"_blank\">interview</a>. That's right, they're bring the unmentionable book back</div> </div> </div> </div>I was lost in rage, confusion and utter bewilderment for ten whole minutes upon reading this.<br /> <br /> I...I don't understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T01:32:31-07:00","id":979552,"title":"","content":"They are very confused - on one hand they are stating 'we will be more diverse and open to all people playing'. On other - we will remake 'Gypsies' book. Well, I'm less social justice oriented to RPG books ( I even liked some one dimensional stereotypes in first 'Gypsies' when I was teen, even when now I all for CoD inclusion model ), but re-opening whole can of worms<i> once again</i>, in this age? I will be shocked if newest edition of WoD will go to end of it's remake cycle for all corebooks after this thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Social Justice Warriors will just <i>eat</i> this this idea - and then writtien book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T03:32:39-07:00","id":979571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979552#post979552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are very confused - on one hand they are stating 'we will be more diverse and open to all people playing'. On other - we will remake 'Gypsies' book. Well, I'm less social justice oriented to RPG books ( I even liked some one dimensional stereotypes in first 'Gypsies' when I was teen, even when now I all for CoD inclusion model ), but re-opening whole can of worms<i> once again</i>, in this age? I will be shocked if newest edition of WoD will go to end of it's remake cycle for all corebooks after this thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Social Justice Warriors will just <i>eat</i> this this idea - and then writtien book.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, they'll need to watch their steps if they don't want to repeat the same mistakes. That said, I've always thought that using Dementation 1 in downtown Athens (since I live there, I know) could always backfire and result in a Humanity-threatening suicide or knife attack. It will be that gentle push <i>too far</i> for some of those most affected by the crisis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T03:35:47-07:00","id":979572,"title":"","content":"This all seems... rather uncharitable.<br /> <br /> Martin wants to have content that highlights the current wave of nationalism and fascism in Europe.<br /> <br /> Martin wants to accomplish this by updating books that touch on very visible minorities that have been historically oppressed by such forces (not exclusively).<br /> <br /> Martin has made it clear that he wants to avoid the mistakes of the past by ensuring the people that write this content are the people that know this content (or as it was phrased can speak to it with credible authenticity).<br /> <br /> Or more simply, he wants to do WOD: Rom correctly, not republish the mess that was WOD: G with updated mechanics.<br /> <br /> If he manages to do it right? Good for him. But it's pretty clear he gets defensive (and then tends to phrase things poorly at best) when people suggest he shouldn't even try.<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> I mean, I get it, this is the CofD section of the forum, and the new WW's choice to focus on the WoD is inherently going to sour CofD primary fans on what they're trying to do. They've stumbled repeatedly in public statements over the reasons for that choice. But is there really a need to turn everything they say into the worst possible reading? It's bad enough that it eats up every other thread about this stuff on the forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:45:05-07:00","id":979627,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be honest. I don't like this new direction White Wolf is taking under Paradox's control. They seem stuck in the past and desperate to cling onto oWoD nostalgia fans instead of helping nWoD/CofD grow as a brand. In all honesty, while the tabletop gaming market was smaller in 2004 than it was in 1991, what hurt Requiem and the other nWoD/CofD lines the most was the mismanagement of White Wolf as a whole under CCP. CCP neglected the brand and let WW die on the vine. So, initially I thought Paradox buying WW was going to be awesome until I found out more of what that actually entails.<br /> <br /> \u200bBetween the decision to resume the oWoD metaplot and scrap the metaplot-neutral nature of the 20th Anniversary editions, as well as include events such as 9/11 into said metaplot, combined with the decision to intentionally sabotage and diminish CofD as a brand so they can promote their &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; by pandering to those blinded by nostalgia and knee-jerk distaste of anything nWoD. I mean, I like Masquerade (sans the metaplot) but I prefer Requiem. Same goes for most of the CofD gamelines, with the noted exception of Demon, as I dislike both Fallen and Descent (nothing wrong with those games per se, but they aren't really my cup of tea)<br /> <br /> And as a disenfranchised former WoD LARP'er, I can attest to that. So, I'll tell you a story about my experiences here in Virginia that is relevant to my point.<br /> <br /> I'm a Requiem fan but the Roanoke VA LARP and White Wolf scene is dominated by hardcore oWoD fans who despise nWoD/CofD just because it's not the game they played back in 1996. For example, when Mind's Eye Society finally established a joint Roanoke/New River Valley-based chapter, the MES people from New River Valley (mostly college girls my age from the college towns of Blacksburg and Radford) initially wanted to do a nWoD Accord venue chronicle, even hosting a regional event for it in March of 2014 at a local Holiday Inn. I was in attendance and I played an Italian-American Daeva in the Circle of the Crone who was a devout Roman polytheist by the name of Tony Cardona, I even dressed up in-character for the occasion. But the Roanoke gamers, being the hardcore oWoD fans they were, threw a huge fit after the LARP, enraged that MES dared to run a nWoD game in the Roanoke Valley. So, while there is still a Mind's Eye Society chapter in Roanoke and the New River Valley, it is exclusively oWoD, only playing the Masquerade and Apocalypse venues. In our particular group, my fellow Millennials were outnumbered by bitter Gen X gamers blinded by nostalgia. So I decided not to officially register with MES, at least not in the Roanoke/New River Valley chapter. It's a shame because my character Tony Cardona was one of my favorite characters I ever made, and I only got to play as him once. Now, if I move to a new area that has a CofD/nWoD friendly Mind's Eye Society chapter, I may officially register with MES and join them. But between the hostility towards nWoD/CofD in my area's gaming scene combined with the fact that I personally dislike By Night Studios' new LARP rules for both mechanical and metaplot reasons, I am done with oWoD LARP, at least organized oWoD LARP.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe thing is, Martin Ericsson and his buddies at the new White Wolf are encouraging and supporting this kind of behavior in the White Wolf fandom. I mean, I'm glad they didn't totally cancel CofD and let Onyx Path continue developing it, but I also resent the fact that they treat Requiem and the like as a red-headed stepchild while promoting a franchise that simply isn't market viable in this day and age without having to rely on nostalgic pandering and attempting to be &quot;edgy&quot;. What worked in the 1990's probably isn't going to work in the 2010's.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, while I do play homebrewed oWoD games that lack metaplot, overall I prefer nWoD/CofD because I don't need to homebrew it nearly as much as I do oWoD in order for me to enjoy it. And some CofD games such as Hunter: The Vigil I don't feel the need to homebrew at all. I like telling my own story rather than the story White Wolf is pushing on me, so I naturally prefer CofD over oWoD.<br /> <br /> \u200bCofD has a lot of potential as a brand precisely because it has no metaplot. Maybe not for Netflix TV shows or anything like that, but it would be great for video games and maybe even novels and comics as well. I mean Bloodlines was a great oWoD video game and as far as I can remember, it didn't really use the metaplot for anything beyond Easter Eggs here and there (well, except maybe the Great Leap Outward since Ming Xiao and the Kuei-Jin play a major role in the game, but that's really the extent of it). Hell, few if any of the metaplot characters from &quot;Los Angeles by Night&quot; are even mentioned in Bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:07:32-07:00","id":979662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979527#post979527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being perfectly honest, our Paradox overlords seem to be stuck in the past. Time will tell if that pays out or not, but even as a punk born too late, I've <b>yet to hear anything</b> from Paradox <b>that inspires me to care</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the punkest thing you could say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:18:13-07:00","id":979673,"title":"","content":"I think it's definitely a generational thing.<br /> <br /> The WoD is about seeing injustice and being angry about it. It's about us vs. them: good (but conflicted) heroes lashing out at a corrupt machine. That's very reflective of the sort of youth political philosophies of the 80s and 90s. It's fun, but it misses a lot of subtleties about how injustice and corruption actually insinuate themselves into society.<br /> <br /> My generation (at least from my experience) tends to focus more on the roots of these problems. Racism is less about mustache twirling KKK members manipulating politics and more about the subconscious and internalized prejudices everyone, knowingly or not, perpetuate. It's about profit-based incarceration. Millenials seem more apt to recognize a philosophy where we all contribute to that machine. They look at this year's presidential election and the question isn't Trump vs. Clinton. It's whether the disproportionate cost disenfranchised groups would have to pay for a Trump election is worth the cost of perpetuating an unfair two party system that we've all helped perpetuate. And I think ChroD does a good job of reflecting those kinds of shaded questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:27:13-07:00","id":979675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979673#post979673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's definitely a generational thing.<br /> <br /> The WoD is about seeing injustice and being angry about it. It's about us vs. them: good (but conflicted) heroes lashing out at a corrupt machine. That's very reflective of the sort of youth political philosophies of the 80s and 90s. It's fun, but it misses a lot of subtleties about how injustice and corruption actually insinuate themselves into society.<br /> <br /> My generation (at least from my experience) tends to focus more on the roots of these problems. Racism is less about mustache twirling KKK members manipulating politics and more about the subconscious and internalized prejudices everyone, knowingly or not, perpetuate. It's about profit-based incarceration. Millenials seem more apt to recognize a philosophy where we all contribute to that machine. They look at this year's presidential election and the question isn't Trump vs. Clinton. It's whether the disproportionate cost disenfranchised groups would have to pay for a Trump election is worth the cost of perpetuating an unfair two party system that we've all helped perpetuate. And I think ChroD does a good job of reflecting those kinds of shaded questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a very nuanced perspective, and is kind of wrong. You're looking at a single subculture and expanding its views over an entire generation, and I'm pretty sure you have the subculture's views wrong. There's plenty of gen Xers who are and were aware of the &quot;roots of these problems&quot; and there are plenty of millennials who miss a lot of subtleties about injustice and corruption. The idea that racism is about mustache twirling KKK members is more a thing that white people do (view racism as super evil done by super evil people) to avoid facing their own racism (and before you say anything, I'm white), and happens across multiple generations.<br /> <br /> As far as identifying the systems of oppression, I recommend looking up Jello Biafra, who as a punk musician in the 70s onward has highlighted these things in his work. Or bell hooks, who wrote extensively on racism and sexism in the 80s and afterward. While both Biafra and bell hooks were born in the 50s, a significant amount of their work was done during the time period you identify as &quot;generation X.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean I think you're onto something here wrt how White Wolf is approaching this stuff, but I wouldn't apply it to an entire generation like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-01-2016, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:49:29-07:00","id":979688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979662#post979662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the punkest thing you could say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I just don't get punk, but I'm pretty sure being uninspired and not caring is not a punk thing. Like, on the contrary, punk is a subculture defined by its passions.<br /> <br /> Not to say Arc isn't punk, just that that particular quote doesn't scream punk to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:54:53-07:00","id":979690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979675#post979675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not a very nuanced perspective, and is kind of wrong. You're looking at a single subculture and expanding its views over an entire generation, and I'm pretty sure you have the subculture's views wrong. There's plenty of gen Xers who are and were aware of the &quot;roots of these problems&quot; and there are plenty of millennials who miss a lot of subtleties about injustice and corruption. The idea that racism is about mustache twirling KKK members is more a thing that white people do (view racism as super evil done by super evil people) to avoid facing their own racism (and before you say anything, I'm white), and happens across multiple generations.<br /> <br /> As far as identifying the systems of oppression, I recommend looking up Jello Biafra, who as a punk musician in the 70s onward has highlighted these things in his work. Or bell hooks, who wrote extensively on racism and sexism in the 80s and afterward. While both Biafra and bell hooks were born in the 50s, a significant amount of their work was done during the time period you identify as &quot;generation X.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean I think you're onto something here wrt how White Wolf is approaching this stuff, but I wouldn't apply it to an entire generation like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love bell hooks and Biafra. Love them to pieces. Although, I saw bell hooks a few months ago, and she seems a little behind the curve regarding a number of contemporary feminist principles like the role of transwomen in the femini<br /> <br /> And you're absolutely right. It was a blanket statement and one that doesn't reflect everyone, but I'm speaking more to the generational aspect of WoD/ChroD players than to the entire social strata.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is more of a white people thing (I'm also white), but I don't hold that against people. If you don't see injustice first hand, you're less likely to understand its intricacies. I do think that more nuanced view of social injustice is more prevalently represented today, but I think that has a lot to do with social media and the opening up greater opportunities for conversation between people of color and other disenfranchised groups and those of us who are more privileged for any variety of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:59:11-07:00","id":979692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979688#post979688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I just don't get punk, but I'm pretty sure being uninspired and not caring is not a punk thing. Like, on the contrary, punk is a subculture defined by its passions.<br /> <br /> Not to say Arc isn't punk, just that that particular quote doesn't scream punk to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm just being cheeky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:07:01-07:00","id":979701,"title":"","content":"Milennials don't have a monopoly on system-level views on social injustice. In fact, most of us learned it from gen X and boomer teachers and professors. That's not what I was trying to express by saying White Wolf has a generational bias. I was referring to Martin's comment about WoD having an impact on people's identities to a greater extent than CofD did. Which is probably true of most people who were playing WoD in high school and/or college, because those are periods in our lives most critical to developing our identities. The comment belies an ignorance of people who were in those formative periods at a time when WoD was a dead game, and CofD was in its heyday. Or if not ignorance, at least dismissal. That's not the audience they're interested in targeting. And frankly, I'm ok with that. I've been consistently wowed by everything Onyx Path has done with Chronicles of Darkness, and consistently unimpressed by everything White Wolf has pitched regarding World of Darkness, so the fact that they're leaving their hands off of CofD and letting OPP take the reigns is a blessing in disguise. It would be nice if they would take greater care when talking about ChroD, as I feel Martin did in this Q&amp;A and Shane did not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:07:36-07:00","id":979702,"title":"","content":"Personally i agree with the interview part of NwoD was conceive as game first and a world second. The first 4 lines pretty much were set in a standard that they had to follow up and push some fluffy pieces to flimsily justify its implementation. The Clan/covenant/bloodline model that sometimes seem pointless in 1st edition, like implementing the 5 classes to everything (warrior, social, thinker, sneaky, etc classes of pc). So NWoD never felts as organic as OWoD, it took Chrod and lots of work from the DM to make it so. The justifications of 1st edition of why there is warrior auspice and a warrior tribe is flimsy so is the fluffy pieces as to why the unecesary paths of mage are there.<br /> <br /> Not saying the other approach was better mind you. Mage ascension had the big problem that the &quot;player party&quot; didnt fit in the setting. Like the mage &quot;society&quot;, game didnt really factor a cabal of various traditions. Vampire coteries always felt weird, and out of place in masquerade. There is sweet middle point between the 2 extremes of NWoD (1st) and OWoD.<br /> <br /> I would never understand the &quot;limiting metaplot&quot; angle of OWoD though, i dont see either line (Chrod and OWoD) as limiting with the exception that OWoD gives me a default setting to fall back into when i wanna change it when Chrod doesnt. I mean if i wanna screw the metaplot and make a caitiff city i can just do it, i would have to pitch that game to my players beforehand but i dont see it how the metaplot would limit me?<br /> <br /> Aside from that i just dont like the direction they say they are taking OWoD. Example i dont agree with their definition of werewolf. To me apocalypse was never about fighting the wyrm or ecoterrorism. The wyrm wasnt never the true antagonist but the garou nation. The Wyrm is too impersonal to be so, its like the zombies in walking dead. The zombies arent the true antagonist but the narrative excuse for your character to having to deal with the ugliest part of the garou nation and try to work with them and slowly change them.<br /> <br /> Same with Ascension, which is to me as whole is a perfect analogy for the 90s. You start (1st edition) all full of piss and passive aggressive vinegar to fight the MAN! because like you know the MAN! want to kill imagination and magic and all those things that are incredible important to people in semigood economic status and the MAN! is evil, fascist and faceless sellouts. Then as the edition/time passes you realize that the MAN! wasnt as faceless or fascist and you though and they were just trying to fix the world as they know how, and you little cliche of fellows dissenters wasnt as pure and righteous as you though.<br /> <br /> Then you grow up and find out that fighting the MAN is not gonna change the world and the world doesnt wanna be change either it like its mediocrity as its stand and the MAN! neither does know what to do because its made up fallible people just like you and is as lost as you are. So you face a choice, do you grow up and try to work with the man and try the hard work of improving the world a little (meaning cooperating with the technocracy not joining)? Do you just give up and live your life without bothering anyone? Or do you stay in your teenage fantasy and keep fighting the man as manchild that can accept the world is more complex (rogue council)?<br /> <br /> Then i found out that that whole thing was completely by accident and the writers always intended for the MAN! to be faceless and authoritarian. The players saw deeper meaning and the steps were taken for it to never happen again. Kinda of sound like the Star Wars special editions doesnt it?<br /> <br /> So honestly i dont care if they &quot;ruin&quot; the setting as long as they give us a good rule set. Its all i ask for. I will ignore the setting they sell me and keep the good rules because while i like WoD and Chrod, their math on the systems leaves a lot to be desired.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-01-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:08:12-07:00","id":979704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979690#post979690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love bell hooks and Biafra. Love them to pieces. Although, I saw bell hooks a few months ago, and she seems a little behind the curve regarding a number of contemporary feminist principles like the role of transwomen in the femini<br /> <br /> And you're absolutely right. It was a blanket statement and one that doesn't reflect everyone, but I'm speaking more to the generational aspect of WoD/ChroD players than to the entire social strata.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is more of a white people thing (I'm also white), but I don't hold that against people. If you don't see injustice first hand, you're less likely to understand its intricacies. I do think that more nuanced view of social injustice is more prevalently represented today, but I think that has a lot to do with social media and the opening up greater opportunities for conversation between people of color and other disenfranchised groups and those of us who are more privileged for any variety of reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd agree bell hooks is falling behind. Some of her comments about Laverne Cox, for example, were pretty bad.<br /> <br /> I also agree that there is a more nuanced view of social injustice over a wider spectrum of people thanks to social media in specific and the internet in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:06:19-07:00","id":979741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979704#post979704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'd agree bell hooks is falling behind. Some of her comments about Laverne Cox, for example, were pretty bad.<br /> <br /> I also agree that there is a more nuanced view of social injustice over a wider spectrum of people thanks to social media in specific and the internet in general.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. I wasn't trying to knock gen x'ers at all. I kind of straddle those two generations myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:41:28-07:00","id":979859,"title":"","content":"I many of the people in this thread are too much in an academic/activist bubble to understand the current generation, especially the working class elements.<br /> <br /> Amoung millenials the Libertarian Candiate is far more popular then Trump, and could be a serious challenge to Hillary amoung millenials and even the green candiate has a solid 10%.<br /> <br /> Will say this generation is more tolerant, but beyond that their is extreme divergiences, they can't be neatly packaged.<br /> <br /> To understand Millenials is to understand the different factions with in it and to understand that brand loyalty is dying concept amoung them, something they encourage in order generations.<br /> <br /> Its made politics far less predictable, then the old broad groupings of the right and left, the whole politucal spectum, social and economic has fractured amoung millenials.<br /> <br /> People as diverse as Milo, Kim Kardasian, Rihanna, the honey badgers, Lacey Green, and Anita Saskesian represent millenial views.<br /> <br /> But none of this really has any fucking thing to do with OWOD vs NWOD vs CoD.<br /> <br /> Really its about Rigid Overarching Metaplot vs. Sandbox mostly metaplot free vs. Refined Sandbox with regional metaplots.<br /> <br /> So I don't see it as generational at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:48:12-07:00","id":979862,"title":"","content":"Edit: Irrelevant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T10:44:58-07:00","id":980331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979301#post979301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: WoD having made a meaningful impact on people's lives and identities in a way that ChroD hasn't to the same extent, this just speaks to a bias towards a particular generation of gamers. Maybe that's true for people who were in high school or college in the 90s, but us millennials weren't playing Masquerade in our formative years, we were playing Requiem. To be fair, tabletop gaming was bigger in the 90s, so there probably is some truth to the idea that WoD may have had that kind of impact on a greater number of people's lives. And that may have been what he meant when he added &quot;to the same extent&quot;.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. While I agree that Martin comes off so Gen X that it hurts, and the OWoD definitely has conceptual and thematic roots in that peculiar and dated cultural moment, most Millennial gamers I know played Masquerade. Like me, they didn't get into it until it was ending or already finished, but they held Requiem and Masquerade up side by side and chose Masquerade. That's not meant as any kind of dig on Requiem or suggesting that Millennial gamers everywhere had this preference, but there's not a neat generational cutoff for OWoD vs NWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T11:30:44-07:00","id":980355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980331#post980331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no. While I agree that Martin comes off so Gen X that it hurts, and the OWoD definitely has conceptual and thematic roots in that peculiar and dated cultural moment, most Millennial gamers I know played Masquerade. Like me, they didn't get into it until it was ending or already finished, but they held Requiem and Masquerade up side by side and chose Masquerade. That's not meant as any kind of dig on Requiem or suggesting that Millennial gamers everywhere had this preference, but there's not a neat generational cutoff for OWoD vs NWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal experiences are personal. Folks you know played Masquerade, I and folks I know played Requiem. I know Gen X folks who dropped Masquerade for Requiem too. I didn't mean that it was a hard cutoff, just that the assertion he made seems either ignorant or dismissive of the fact that there is a whole generation to whom old World of Darkness was a grognard's game and new World of Darkness was the new hotness.<br /> <br /> Personally, I started looking into the games because I saw the books on the shelves at the game store where I played Friday Night Magic. Did the research, found out there were two Worlds of Darkness, the old and the new. And, based on my experience with D&amp;D, where 3.5 was an overcomplicated mess played by gamers who were bitter about the new edition and 4E was an easily accessible game who's haters' consistent critique was &quot;It's a good game, it's just not D&amp;D&quot;, I saw an obvious parallel. As a 4E player myself at the time, I picked up nWoD without a second thought. And while my view of both 3.5 and of cWoD at the time was undeservedly harsh, I have never regretted the decision to adopt the newer games over the old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-02-2016, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T16:22:36-07:00","id":980465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980355#post980355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personal experiences are personal. Folks you know played Masquerade, I and folks I know played Requiem. I know Gen X folks who dropped Masquerade for Requiem too. I didn't mean that it was a hard cutoff, just that the assertion he made seems either ignorant or dismissive of the fact that there is a whole generation to whom old World of Darkness was a grognard's game and new World of Darkness was the new hotness.<br /> <br /> Personally, I started looking into the games because I saw the books on the shelves at the game store where I played Friday Night Magic. Did the research, found out there were two Worlds of Darkness, the old and the new. And, based on my experience with D&amp;D, where 3.5 was an overcomplicated mess played by gamers who were bitter about the new edition and 4E was an easily accessible game who's haters' consistent critique was &amp;quot;It's a good game, it's just not D&amp;D&amp;quot;, I saw an obvious parallel. As a 4E player myself at the time, I picked up nWoD without a second thought. And while my view of both 3.5 and of cWoD at the time was undeservedly harsh, I have never regretted the decision to adopt the newer games over the old.</div> </div> </div> </div> Now its 4e in 3.5 position and 5e is the new hotness (even if its poorly supported compared to 4e).<br /> <br /> For the record I'm on the cusp between the 2 generations, born 1979, so I feel like I truely belong to neither.<br /> <br /> I think people over state generational difference and make far to many generalizations about a generation, they reflect themselves more then the generation they're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T16:40:13-07:00","id":980469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979627#post979627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as a disenfranchised former WoD LARP'er, I can attest to that. So, I'll tell you a story about my experiences here in Virginia that is relevant to my point.<br /> <br /> I'm a Requiem fan but the Roanoke VA LARP and White Wolf scene is dominated by hardcore oWoD fans who despise nWoD/CofD just because it's not the game they played back in 1996. For example, when Mind's Eye Society finally established a joint Roanoke/New River Valley-based chapter, the MES people from New River Valley (mostly college girls my age from the college towns of Blacksburg and Radford) initially wanted to do a nWoD Accord venue chronicle, even hosting a regional event for it in March of 2014 at a local Holiday Inn. I was in attendance and I played an Italian-American Daeva in the Circle of the Crone who was a devout Roman polytheist by the name of Tony Cardona, I even dressed up in-character for the occasion. But the Roanoke gamers, being the hardcore oWoD fans they were, threw a huge fit after the LARP, enraged that MES dared to run a nWoD game in the Roanoke Valley. So, while there is still a Mind's Eye Society chapter in Roanoke and the New River Valley, it is exclusively oWoD, only playing the Masquerade and Apocalypse venues. In our particular group, my fellow Millennials were outnumbered by bitter Gen X gamers blinded by nostalgia. So I decided not to officially register with MES, at least not in the Roanoke/New River Valley chapter. It's a shame because my character Tony Cardona was one of my favorite characters I ever made, and I only got to play as him once. Now, if I move to a new area that has a CofD/nWoD friendly Mind's Eye Society chapter, I may officially register with MES and join them. But between the hostility towards nWoD/CofD in my area's gaming scene combined with the fact that I personally dislike By Night Studios' new LARP rules for both mechanical and metaplot reasons, I am done with oWoD LARP, at least organized oWoD LARP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you checked out any of the MES troupes in northern VA and central MD? NWoD makes up more than half the total MES games there. <br /> <br /> I won't dispute however that there exist frustrating OWoD partisans who refuse to even acknowledge or entertain the NWoD for reasons I can't begin to fathom. That being said, a number of gamers I know who used to fit that description have since come around to being NWoD fans as well, so even then there exists the possibility for everyone to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:01:12-07:00","id":980477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980465#post980465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now its 4e in 3.5 position and 5e is the new hotness (even if its poorly supported compared to 4e).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, totally. I play 5E now when I play D&amp;D. 4E was a big improvement over 3.X in my opinion, but it was deeply flawed in all new ways. 5E just abandons 4E's design lessons almost entirely, which is a shame cause it threw the baby out with the bath water. I'd love to see a D&amp;D that combines the best parts of both edition's designs, but between the two I ultimately prefer 5E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:42:24-07:00","id":980498,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, I feel similarly, but that places me on 4E's side. 4E was not necessarily a successful experiment for DnD, but it tried to solve some of the longest standing problems with Dungeons and Dragons and the d20 system and actually succeeded in some interesting ways that would have been great to see be built upon.<br /> <br /> 5E was a total and completely abandonment from that spirit of improvement, instead relying of the comfort and security of &quot;improving&quot; on where 3.5 left off. I say &quot;improving&quot; because while it does streamline and smooth out certain parts, it actually makes some of the big flaming messes that 3.5 had worse (Which is frustrating to see considering some of them were resolved by 4E.) If I wanted a better version of 3.5, I'd play Pathfinder(and I still don't like Pathfinder, mind) which actually <i>did</i> improve on the experience of 3.5(broken as shit as that experience is), whereas 5E isn't anything except a completely ballsless retreat from fan backlash rather than an actual attempt to learn from lessons and continuing to try and innovate.<br /> <br /> Yeah, 4E has a lot of problems, but given what I go to DnD for, I'll take it's failures in experimentation over a completely gutless retreat. (Well, that, and I think the failures don't quite outweigh the successes of 4E for me in terms of the kind of games I go looking for if I ever go to DnD, rare experience though that might be today.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-02-2016, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:55:28-07:00","id":980501,"title":"","content":"I saw the D&amp;D conversation and wanted to get involved, but Arc basically said what I would have, only good 'cuz he's a writer and I'm a coder.<br /> <br /> Did not care for Shane's comments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T18:56:28-07:00","id":980513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980498#post980498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funnily enough, I feel similarly, but that places me on 4E's side. 4E was not necessarily a successful experiment for DnD, but it tried to solve some of the longest standing problems with Dungeons and Dragons and the d20 system and actually succeeded in some interesting ways that would have been great to see be built upon.<br /> <br /> 5E was a total and completely abandonment from that spirit of improvement, instead relying of the comfort and security of &quot;improving&quot; on where 3.5 left off. I say &quot;improving&quot; because while it does streamline and smooth out certain parts, it actually makes some of the big flaming messes that 3.5 had worse (Which is frustrating to see considering some of them were resolved by 4E.) If I wanted a better version of 3.5, I'd play Pathfinder(and I still don't like Pathfinder, mind) which actually <i>did</i> improve on the experience of 3.5(broken as shit as that experience is), whereas 5E isn't anything except a completely ballsless retreat from fan backlash rather than an actual attempt to learn from lessons and continuing to try and innovate.<br /> <br /> Yeah, 4E has a lot of problems, but given what I go to DnD for, I'll take it's failures in experimentation over a completely gutless retreat. (Well, that, and I think the failures don't quite outweigh the successes of 4E for me in terms of the kind of games I go looking for if I ever go to DnD, rare experience though that might be today.)</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of dragging this tangent out further, I agree, for the most part. Even if 4E isn't my cup of tea any more, I respect its boldness far more than 5E, which looked promising early in the open development process when they were pontificating on modular design and looking at sacred cows with a critical eye, but got steadily safer with every playtest packet (as though any other outcome could come of what amounted to crowdsourced design).<br /> <br /> What I would most like to see in D&amp;D is something along the lines of an evolution of the 4E Essentials line. Essentials fixed the majority of my gripes with 4E, but it didn't get much support before they killed the edition - plus it came saddled with the rest of 4E, and having Essentials characters in the same games as pre-Essentials 4E characters never quite worked. My dream D&amp;D would be something with an Essentials-like PC powers design, 4E's monster and encounter design, D&amp;D Next's original concept of bounded accuracy (which even 5E didn't end up committing to), 5E's magic-items-as-reward approach to loot as opposed to 4E's magic-items-as-advancement approach (probably my single biggest gripe with 4E), and maybe 13th Age's backgrounds-as-skills system. Bonus points if it could ditch the ability score/ability bonus divide (I can dream, can't I?). But, as cowardly as 5E's design is, I'll take it over Pathfinder (which isn't <i>as bad</i> as 3.5 but is still far too fiddly for what I want out of D&amp;D) or 4E's loot treadmill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-02-2016, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:08:16-07:00","id":980517,"title":"","content":"I could have whole discussions about the problem of DnD, particularly when you consider the problem of 3.5(seriously, that incarnation is going to be the cause of spiralling deficiencies in DnD from here on out until someone finally breaks the whole damn thing) and the question of what sort of game DnD really is.<br /> <br /> But while a relevant analogue for what Paradox is doing, it is getting a little off base. Besides, there are other things to burn on the discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:25:15-07:00","id":980522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980498#post980498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll take it's failures in experimentation over a completely gutless retreat. (Well, that, and I think the failures don't quite outweigh the successes of 4E for me in terms of the kind of games I go looking for if I ever go to DnD, rare experience though that might be today.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Im on the opposite camp there, i feel that sometimes people overglorify creator vision as inherently better. If people want D&amp;D to be confort food then its not an inherently bad choice to follow through with that.<br /> <br /> Same with WoD, when in mage they &quot;blew&quot; the umbra because the player base play the game differently of what they creators invisioned seem ill conceive to me. Same with the technocracy as the dev getting angry that a big chunk of the player base interpret the exact opposite of what they want, fortunately in that case they relented on mage itself but them took step for it to never happen again.<br /> <br /> i take a safe game over a &quot;you play my vision and nothing else&quot; kind of game.<br /> <br /> A spot on example of creative vision not working is the whole Star Wars special editions. George Lucas has an artistic &quot;vision&quot; of how the movies should be and the fans have another. George Lucas kept ignoring the fans to follow with the vision in an unreasonable way as he could have release unmodified and modified versions.<br /> <br /> Now disney has the right and pretty much sold the unmodified version as that what people want along with the modified to cater to all fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-02-2016, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:32:08-07:00","id":980528,"title":"","content":"Man, I wonder if Dave regrets making that comment about the Technocracy. People sure seem to love referencing it like it's some damning critique of Onyx Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:42:12-07:00","id":980533,"title":"","content":"I think people are definitely reading a lot into Dave's statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:59:52-07:00","id":980539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980528#post980528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I wonder if Dave regrets making that comment about the Technocracy. People sure seem to love referencing it like it's some damning critique of Onyx Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats most obvious example mind you, there that whole condescending vibe all through revised like &quot;here is the rules for X thing, you should never allow it because ANY player asking to play this is obviously a munchkin&quot; Lots of book in revised had a bitter tone of the authors being piss off that the fan played the games in ways they didnt like. Or maybe i got the &quot;bitter book&quot; in my read of<br /> <br /> CoG revised another example of a book in dire need of someone restraining the &quot;vision&quot; of its author.<br /> <br /> The whole technocracy comment though, damm, that is baffling on 10 kinds of levels. Not only does it show a failure of communication on the intent of the book but fans interpreted something completely opposite to that and though it was brilliant. And the developers got mad about it is the cherry on that because their original vision was &quot;bad&quot; (in the sense that we had 2 editions with irredeemable black hats technocracy and people took morally complex technocrat almost unanimously)<br /> <br /> I got a degree in business and what they taught us is that when by sheer miracle the buying public missinterpret your idea for another and they think is brilliant (which prove in this particular case the original one wasnt gonna be that good) then you dont get mad. You cash on that and pretend it was the plan all along. Not taking steps for said miracle to never happen again.<br /> <br /> Is like trying to produce the virtual boy, then by accident producing the PS2. People commenting how they love the PS2 and saying &quot;good they didnt made some sort of ill-conceived VR console&quot; leaving the question of whether the another one was gonna be more like or not not rest. And then on the next board meeting say &quot;okay guys, we know we accidentally made the PS2 and people love it but we have to take step to never do a PS2 ever again. If we wanna do the sega dreamcast we made the sega dreamcast and stop any chance of making the iphone by accident&quot;<br /> <br /> As for it is a damming critique or not on onyxpath (which to be fair this happened when it was white wolf) *shrugs* on one hand that kind of thinking leaves me to think that maybe OWoD is better off with another company with less creativity and more bussiness savy (though if paradox is that company is still not clear) and what a i liked about WoD so far is my interpretation and the reality is far simpler and boring.<br /> <br /> Maybe WtA wasnt a perfect analogy of social movement for a good cause and dealing with extremist of good causes who are assholes and instead was just furry ecoterrorist captain planet all along?<br /> <br /> Maybe the overglofication of pointless sacrifice was to be taken at face value all along too?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i50.photobucket.com/albums/f339/TrickeryandLies/You%20Know/Fandom%20Macros%20and%20Gifs/tumblr_m2ywesXtQ41qk7wyq.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> On the other hand i still keep buying the book so what do i know? Maybe that as sign that their bussiness savy is more superior to anything i can understand<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-02-2016, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:18:44-07:00","id":980547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980522#post980522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im on the opposite camp there, i feel that sometimes people overglorify creator vision as inherently better. If people want D&amp;D to be confort food then its not an inherently bad choice to follow through with that.<br /> <br /> Same with WoD, when in mage they &quot;blew&quot; the umbra because the player base play the game differently of what they creators invisioned seem ill conceive to me. Same with the technocracy as the dev getting angry that a big chunk of the player base interpret the exact opposite of what they want, fortunately in that case they relented on mage itself but them took step for it to never happen again.<br /> <br /> i take a safe game over a &quot;you play my vision and nothing else&quot; kind of game.<br /> <br /> A spot on example of creative vision not working is the whole Star Wars special editions. George Lucas has an artistic &quot;vision&quot; of how the movies should be and the fans have another. George Lucas kept ignoring the fans to follow with the vision in an unreasonable way as he could have release unmodified and modified versions.<br /> <br /> Now disney has the right and pretty much sold the unmodified version as that what people want along with the modified to cater to all fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>My position is not that creator vision is inherently better. I've argued with creators enough to know that.<br /> <br /> Not, mind you, that fan vision is better. Fans have demonstrated to me, across several fandoms, that they have just as much propensity for not knowing what they are talking about as creators.<br /> <br /> Really, the nature of the subject is not about the spectrum between creators and fandoms, as far as this goes. I have some very strong opinions on the subject, of course, but that wasn't what I was talking about.<br /> <br /> DnD 3.5 hit a ceiling in ways-in many ways, it was as good as DnD was going to be without challenging some of it's core assumptions. This didn't make it a good game-it's very clearly a flawed game. Pathfinder and DnD 4th are flawed games that nevertheless did more with what DnD could be based on how you read the game and how you focused it. They demonstrably tried to make DnD a better game.<br /> <br /> DnD 5E's problem is that it didn't really to try to make DnD a better game, learning from the advancements that worked in 4th and Pathfinder and some of it's other contemporaries. It's main concern was simply backpedaling from the fact that 4E was a big commercial failure (a fact even I will cop to) and appealing to it's fanbase <i>without</i> really trying to continue advancing the game.<br /> <br /> My problem is not that there was not a gun-sticking to creator vision, but that there was a failure to significantly improve the game through experimentation. The fact that this is done as a fear response to the fanbase, while understandable from a business standpoint, just makes it more annoying.<br /> <br /> Appeasement is a factor for businesses, and really a certain amount of that is always going to be needed for any kind of communication, but it shouldn't come at the cost of <i>improving your product</i>. 5E has done very little to try and improve it's product, and actively made it worse in a number of ways.<br /> <br /> As for the Guide to the Technocracy. There were significant problems with the fanbase framing the Technocracy as equally good choices for players as the Traditions, and where GttT could have cleared that up, it instead just muddled the issue further and increased the popularity of them*. Even disregarding the social impact that came with this and the way this promoted a lot of toxic attitudes on the internet that don't need reinforcing, it also fucked up the White Wolf consumer base's expectations of how all antagonists were supposed to operate. No, dear reader, the Pure are not people you should want to be. No, the Seers are not supposed to be people you'd willingly join. You should dread all the ways you could become them. They should be relatable, understandable-you should look and know all that keeps you from them and how thin a line that actually is. But you should never want <i>to be them</i>.Like, every time I make the point of how so many people would actually be Seers, I don't say that with joy, with an expectation of people thinking they're doing the right thing, that it is a fair and equal thing to the Pentacle Alliance.<br /> <br /> I deeply enjoyed Guide to the Technocracy, and I enjoy the moral ambiguity at work in Ascension with the conflict between the Traditions and the Technocracy, with both sides being genuinely fucked up. I think in a lot of ways Ascension became better when it became clear how everyone's good intentions were going to fuck the world over on every level. But it was, in so many ways, a fuck-up despite every ounce of good that came out of it, and I think as far as fan vs creator conversations go(which is a false dichotomy), it is a clear example of how thorny these subjects can be.<br /> <br /> Because, yeah, in a lot of ways, it made Ascension better, but in a lot of ways, it made Ascension's fanbase worse, and it has proven to be a thorn in the side of the World/Chronicles of Darkness discussions ever since, nevermind wider culture.<br /> <br /> To point out these problems as Dave did is not to go &quot;My Vision or The Highway&quot;. It's to be actually cognizant of the full picture. It's to avoid making really damning mistakes.<br /> <br /> *Keep in mind that I say this as a fan of the Technocracy, as someone who would probably take his chances with all the ways the Technocracy are fucked up and bound to destroy the world and it's agents just for the principle at it's heart worth fighting for that might, just might, find a way to overcome the rotten husk the Technocracy was always bound to become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:27:13-07:00","id":980548,"title":"","content":"I think that a lot of what people saw as heroism or gray morality in the Technocracy was projection more than anything written by the authors. I'm not sure that what the players saw was brilliant so much as wish fulfilment. Which is fine. I didn't really take Dave's comment as being all that bad, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:33:28-07:00","id":980551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980547#post980547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even disregarding the social impact that came with this and the way this promoted a lot of toxic attitudes on the internet that don't need reinforcing,</div> </div> </div> </div>Im curious about this. Can you expand? the book release was 1999 but i picked up about 2010 so im missing a lot of what the internet fandom was back then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980547#post980547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To point out these problems as Dave did is not to go &quot;My Vision or The Highway&quot;. It's to be actually cognizant of the full picture. It's to avoid making really damning mistakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;my vision or the highway&quot; comment i did wasnt directed to the whole guide to the technocracy but the tone many books of Revised took.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-02-2016, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:41:39-07:00","id":980554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980551#post980551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im curious about this. Can you expand? the book release was 1999 but i picked up about 2010 so im missing a lot of what the internet fandom was back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a whole can of worms that I don't have time to go into, nor is this the place for it. For now, I will say that the entire thing is a marvellous example of how good principles can so easily warp into terrible, awful base assumptions when it's not handled properly. As a relevant thought exercise, ask yourself everything the Technocracy does in defense of it's principle of building a better world, then take a long look at what the Technocracy's most hardcore fanbase does in discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:45:26-07:00","id":980556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980477#post980477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, totally. I play 5E now when I play D&amp;D. 4E was a big improvement over 3.X in my opinion, but it was deeply flawed in all new ways. 5E just abandons 4E's design lessons almost entirely, which is a shame cause it threw the baby out with the bath water. I'd love to see a D&amp;D that combines the best parts of both edition's designs, but between the two I ultimately prefer 5E.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love 5E. I don't necessarily love every aspect of it, but as an overall product I adore it. It feels like a greatest hits collection, and I think if you scratch away the top coat you'll find some pieces of 4E rattling around in there. <br /> <br /> I'm genuinely surprised, this is the first new edition of D&amp;D I <i>haven't</i> reflexively irrationally hated. I started at the dawn of new millennium with a 2E starter kit and a bunch of hand-me-down 1E books. It took until winter '02 for 3E to actually find its way to West Virginia and for people I knew to start playing it, and I utterly detested it. It wasn't <i>my</i> D&amp;D! No sir! I categorically refused to play it until about '06, but over time it did slowly grow on me. I didn't love every aspect of it, but as an overall product I came to like it. I had pretty much the same reaction a second time when 4E dropped, albeit with a certain wry amusement that people my age were complaining about it not being &quot;real&quot; D&amp;D. I've given it several tries over the years, but 4E still never really clicked with me. It's hard to say exactly why, but I just don't engage with the system. 5E has the advantage of taking the parts of 4E I liked and throwing them on a mixtape with my old favorites from the previous three editions.<br /> <br /> Like I said, its not perfect. I love the idea of making magic items more unique and story-driven, moving away from the shopping list mentality 3E exemplified, but at the same time its kind of broken their treasure system. I love the concept of the sub-classes, but it does front load a lot of your significant build choices. I love what they've done with Cantrips, but wish they hadn't retreated back into a pseudo-Vancian system again. All that being said, I've had better success recruiting new gamers with 5E than I have with any other edition. <br /> <br /> The best success I and my group have had with 3E has been turning its intense granularity into a world-building feature, using it to probe underlying metaphysical assumptions implied by the mechanics and the socio-cultural implications if said mechanics are taken to logical end points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T21:12:18-07:00","id":980570,"title":"","content":"Umm... I know &quot;4E was a commercial failure&quot; is common knowledge and all, but... It's really not the case... 4E actually outsold 3.5, according to the only people who have access to that data. Where 4E failed was in not meeting Hazbro's projected growth rates for the brand, and in creating its own greatest rival (though the latter was at least as much the fault of the 3.5 OGL as it was of 4E itself.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T21:17:16-07:00","id":980572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980570#post980570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... I know &quot;4E was a commercial failure&quot; is common knowledge and all, but... It's really not the case... 4E actually outsold 3.5, according to the only people who have access to that data. Where 4E failed was in not meeting Hazbro's projected growth rates for the brand, and in creating its own greatest rival (though the latter was at least as much the fault of the 3.5 OGL as it was of 4E itself.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, yes, this is the more accurate portrayal of the scenario, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T22:38:18-07:00","id":980587,"title":"","content":"Everytime I read about the focus on the generation that oWoD spoke to, the more I feel like Martin is speaking to a very narrow fanbase that isn't really a modern one. I'm not excited for Your European Uncle's views on racism in modern Europe. At the very least, I really hope they realize that racial slurs make bad book titles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:17:53-07:00","id":980599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980587#post980587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everytime I read about the focus on the generation that oWoD spoke to, the more I feel like Martin is speaking to a very narrow fanbase that isn't really a modern one. I'm not excited for Your European Uncle's views on racism in modern Europe. At the very least, I really hope they realize that racial slurs make bad book titles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't like this more than once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:55:43-07:00","id":980636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980528#post980528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I wonder if Dave regrets making that comment about the Technocracy. People sure seem to love referencing it like it's some damning critique of Onyx Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it's just LRS letting his biases show.<br /> <br /> I own every Ascension product, down to the coffee mug. I was an Ascension fan for decades. Revised edition is the best, and did a *lot* to grey-hat the Technocracy when it became clear people did not get the joke. Rolling with the punch and calling off the progrom, as it were.<br /> <br /> It's probably the best second edition book. It just suffers from the problem common to its gameline, when received fanwisdom about what's in it is way more important than what's actually in it. Which is so oldMage it hurts.<br /> <br /> Anyways, CofD books aren't written with that kind of unreliable narrator voice, and in the Pure/Seers writing back in 2008 we knew that. We did discuss how to not have Seers get horribly misinterpreted, but the Technocracy wasn't the only earlier villain book we looked for lessons from - fans at the time were really enthused about seeing books in the format of VII (especially, for some reason, the Seers) and we spent wa more time considering and rejecting that approach.<br /> <br /> (The reason being that VII is an awesome book any given chronicle can only use a third of, and prevents any writer from doing anything concrete with VII ever again. It's okay for that one faction, I guess, but I think I'm the only writer to use the buggers since and I had to invent a whole fourth origin/setup for them to do it. It is absolutely not the way to go for the Pure or Seers)<br /> <br /> But ensure we never write another GttT? Nah. One of the first books for Deviant will, White Wolf permitting, be a book for playing their counterparts still working for the conspiracies, slowly realising that they're being used by their masters while hunting Renegades.<br /> <br /> It's just that this time we'll be extra careful to tell the reader what we're trying to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T07:14:59-07:00","id":980758,"title":"","content":"Again, GttT was great for Ascension, not so great for it's fanbase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T08:02:42-07:00","id":980772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980636#post980636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revised edition is the best, and did a *lot* to grey-hat the Technocracy when it became clear people did not get the joke. Rolling with the punch and calling off the progrom, as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting take on it that I hadn't considered before. Are you saying that people not recognizing the satire was a major impetus behind making the Technocracy more playable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T08:08:19-07:00","id":980777,"title":"","content":"The conversation about the Technocracy starting out as a satire that the fans didn't get interests me because it reminds me of the evolution of Warhammer 40K, which from what I understand started out as a satire of over-the-top grimdark 80s comics and sci-fi during the Thatcher Era, but so many fans didn't get it that we now have the even funnier straight take on the setting in the modern day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T08:28:38-07:00","id":980783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980777#post980777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conversation about the Technocracy starting out as a satire that the fans didn't get interests me because it reminds me of the evolution of Warhammer 40K, which from what I understand started out as a satire of over-the-top grimdark 80s comics and sci-fi during the Thatcher Era, but so many fans didn't get it that we now have the even funnier straight take on the setting in the modern day.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something in my gut about how a desire to seek sympathy in a lot of these authoritarian or dystopian ideas is to try and redeem how some parts of them inform a lot of our perspective and policies on contemporary issues. Like we see a part of ourselves in these ideas and so we don't want to reject them out of hand. I think it makes a lot of sense in particular for the Technocracy, and how it's position as the Scientific Establishment (in its worst, most oppressive incarnation) might also be coded by a lot of nerdy folk like us as an elite which has unique knowledge that Everyone Else does not, and because they have a Greater Understanding they're justified.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's a theory that describes this, but the basic idea is that there's an in-group of people who know stuff and everyone else is the ignorant masses, and while usually for nerdy people that's the kind of stuff that structures a persecution complex, for governments, it's the kind of stuff that leads to elite rule, and is often informed by a distrust in the ignorance and lack of expertise in the general populace. Hell, this kind of mentality is a significant one for the founding of the United States!<br /> <br /> I think that is the key to why people like the Technocracy and such. Because they can see them as they see themselves, an intellectual out-group, hard men making hard choices, all that jazz.<br /> <br /> I think it's a Thing in a lot of subcultures, but particularly among people with nerdy hobbies it seems to be big. For another example, see the meme of the &quot;normie&quot; and the like.<br /> <br /> It's interesting because I think this idea is actually pretty intersectional with the punk ideology as well, in the sense that its practice by the out-group of punks predicates on the notion of a mainstream that will not or can't wake up to the things punks find intolerable. Punk seems angry with the system, sure, but it also seems pretty angry with the mainstream for falling in line. Two sides of the same coin? That might be overly reductive, but it's easy to see how this kind of self-conception could feed into adoration for the Anarchs and adoration for the Technocracy at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:15:49-07:00","id":980808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980777#post980777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conversation about the Technocracy starting out as a satire that the fans didn't get interests me because it reminds me of the evolution of Warhammer 40K, which from what I understand started out as a satire of over-the-top grimdark 80s comics and sci-fi during the Thatcher Era, but so many fans didn't get it that we now have the even funnier straight take on the setting in the modern day.</div> </div> </div> </div>My favourite part of Rogue Trader is Birmingham, the black planet where the sun never shines.<br /> <br /> Or is it Imperial Inquisitor Obi-Won Sherlock Cleuso?<br /> <br /> Probably both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:28:55-07:00","id":980819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980498#post980498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funnily enough, I feel similarly, but that places me on 4E's side. 4E was not necessarily a successful experiment for DnD, but it tried to solve some of the longest standing problems with Dungeons and Dragons and the d20 system and actually succeeded in some interesting ways that would have been great to see be built upon.<br /> <br /> 5E was a total and completely abandonment from that spirit of improvement, instead relying of the comfort and security of &quot;improving&quot; on where 3.5 left off. I say &quot;improving&quot; because while it does streamline and smooth out certain parts, it actually makes some of the big flaming messes that 3.5 had worse (Which is frustrating to see considering some of them were resolved by 4E.) If I wanted a better version of 3.5, I'd play Pathfinder(and I still don't like Pathfinder, mind) which actually <i>did</i> improve on the experience of 3.5(broken as shit as that experience is), whereas 5E isn't anything except a completely ballsless retreat from fan backlash rather than an actual attempt to learn from lessons and continuing to try and innovate.<br /> <br /> Yeah, 4E has a lot of problems, but given what I go to DnD for, I'll take it's failures in experimentation over a completely gutless retreat. (Well, that, and I think the failures don't quite outweigh the successes of 4E for me in terms of the kind of games I go looking for if I ever go to DnD, rare experience though that might be today.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af<br /> <br /> That's what you get with Open Dev. The fans spoketh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:08:21-07:00","id":980850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980498#post980498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funnily enough, I feel similarly, but that places me on 4E's side. 4E was not necessarily a successful experiment for DnD, but it tried to solve some of the longest standing problems with Dungeons and Dragons and the d20 system and actually succeeded in some interesting ways that would have been great to see be built upon.<br /> <br /> 5E was a total and completely abandonment from that spirit of improvement, instead relying of the comfort and security of &amp;quot;improving&amp;quot; on where 3.5 left off. I say &amp;quot;improving&amp;quot; because while it does streamline and smooth out certain parts, it actually makes some of the big flaming messes that 3.5 had worse (Which is frustrating to see considering some of them were resolved by 4E.) If I wanted a better version of 3.5, I'd play Pathfinder(and I still don't like Pathfinder, mind) which actually <i>did</i> improve on the experience of 3.5(broken as shit as that experience is), whereas 5E isn't anything except a completely ballsless retreat from fan backlash rather than an actual attempt to learn from lessons and continuing to try and innovate.<br /> <br /> Yeah, 4E has a lot of problems, but given what I go to DnD for, I'll take it's failures in experimentation over a completely gutless retreat. (Well, that, and I think the failures don't quite outweigh the successes of 4E for me in terms of the kind of games I go looking for if I ever go to DnD, rare experience though that might be today.)</div> </div> </div> </div> I liked 4e, but I love 5e because it feels like all the best parts combined, then refined with completely new ideas like bounded accucy and advantage. <br /> <br /> As for pathfinder, I find 5e to be way better, although I like Golarion as a setting and the novels.<br /> <br /> But 5e has elements I really like that aren't present in patheefinder/3.x<br /> <br /> Although I'm interested in they're new spun off Starfinder when it comes out.<br /> <br /> Anyway back to the OWOD vs. CoD brewhaha, that the CEO of White Wolf carelessly started started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:09:31-07:00","id":980853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980777#post980777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conversation about the Technocracy starting out as a satire that the fans didn't get interests me because it reminds me of the evolution of Warhammer 40K, which from what I understand started out as a satire of over-the-top grimdark 80s comics and sci-fi during the Thatcher Era, but so many fans didn't get it that we now have the even funnier straight take on the setting in the modern day.</div> </div> </div> </div>The worst part of 40k is the fanbase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:24:17-07:00","id":980868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980853#post980853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The worst part of 40k is the fanbase.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think that's unique to 40k, I've seen nice fandoms, but I've seen fandoms that get really nasty.<br /> <br /> I can't speak to 40k, I simply couldn't get into warhammer stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:34:46-07:00","id":980876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980554#post980554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a relevant thought exercise, ask yourself everything the Technocracy does in defense of it's principle of building a better world, then take a long look at what the Technocracy's most hardcore fanbase does in discussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean liking the authoritarian political leaning of the organization? Or you mean endless flamewars and bad internet behavior?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980850#post980850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway back to the OWOD vs. CoD brewhaha, that the CEO of White Wolf carelessly started started.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows if it was caressly, maybe it is a marketting ploy to get the bitter over chrod fanbase.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980853#post980853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The worst part of 40k is the fanbase.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also of Dr who, Star Wars, Star Trek, CoD (the videogame), D&amp;D, Shadowrun....etc etc etc. Rabid fanbases are everywhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:35:27-07:00","id":980878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980783#post980783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that is the key to why people like the Technocracy and such. Because they can see them as they see themselves, an intellectual out-group, hard men making hard choices, all that jazz.<br /> <br /> I think it's a Thing in a lot of subcultures, but particularly among people with nerdy hobbies it seems to be big. For another example, see the meme of the &quot;normie&quot; and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be part of it, but I feel like the #1 thing behind the rise of the heroic Technocracy meme stems from rejection of the trappings of the Traditions. A lot of people are viscerally disgusted by the idea of playing a heroic faith healer struggling against the Man and his wicked science, and will start inventing reasons why the Traditions are the bad guys without even realizing they're doing it.<br /> <br /> (Admittedly, most of those reasons are now true, I guess, since M20 made &quot;the Traditions hate light bulbs&quot; canon.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:04:20-07:00","id":980894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980878#post980878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, most of those reasons are now true, I guess, since M20 made &quot;the Traditions hate light bulbs&quot; canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this mean? I played only few sessions in <b>Ascension </b>and I do not understand this sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:47:38-07:00","id":980915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980894#post980894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What does this mean? I played only few sessions in <b>Ascension </b>and I do not understand this sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>One part of what Dave called the &quot;fan understanding&quot; of Ascension was the idea that the Traditions are rabidly reactionary and anti-science, and that their victory over the Technocracy would mean a return to the Dark Ages where wizardry is the only law and flush toilets are forbidden.<br /> <br /> This view was not really supported by the books until M20 decided to include a speech about how, yeah, the Traditions basically are the kind of people who would rather use candles than light bulbs.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm shocked by the amount of effort M20 put into blackwashing the Traditions, because in my view they needed the exact opposite given how unpopular they've become.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:00:57-07:00","id":980923,"title":"","content":"Gonna throw my two cents in the ring as a proponent of the &quot;grey morality&quot; Technocracy. No, I wasn't indulging in pro-science nerd fascist wish fulfillment. I thought the core idea behind the initial formation of the Technocracy, that magic should be made universally accessible rather than being left in the hands of the Enlightened elite to use or abuse as they saw fit, as really interesting given the metaphysics of Mage. I found the concept of an ideological conflict between the Traditions and Technocracy a lot more interesting than rebels fighting the comically overblown Men-in-Black. I had much the same problem with Werewolf. I like nuanced conflicts between potentially sympathetic people to be more interesting than fighting against comic book evil. I acknowledge that this isn't what the writers intended and that's fine. They were going for grey vs. black where I prefer grey vs. grey. Just a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> I don't, though, think that condescending speculation about the psychology of folks such as myself is fruitful. Not picking a fight here, just warning about the dangers of stereotyping. And this brings me back to the actual topic of the thread. Someone I read recently noted that a lot of the problem with discussions is that people assume that other folks have the same priorities as them. This leads to folks tarring those who disagree with them with ridiculous claims like &quot;Republicans hate women&quot; or &quot;Democrats are against religion&quot;. I would simply ask people to recognize that other folks might have different tastes, perspectives, or priorities than themselves.<br /> <br /> Some people roleplay as an escape from their lives, to have fun and lose themselves in a fantasy setting. Some people do it out of a deep desire to explore other perspectives, challenge their preconceptions, and push themselves past their comfort zones. Some people roleplay just to hang out with their friends and be social. Some roleplay because they like problem-solving, tactics, and optimizing their character. Each of these approaches is equally valid but can lead to very different opinions on how games should be designed, run, and enjoyed. It leads to different opinions on what games are good and bad. Ultimately, what games are good or bad isn't an objective measure. It is entirely based on what you are trying to get out of them. And it is worth recognizing that sometimes, a game just isn't for you. Or that a game that you enjoyed is enjoyed by other people for different reasons and they may take it in a different direction than you like. And that's okay. The old books aren't going anywhere.<br /> <br /> Okay, that's longer than I intended it to be and a bit lecture-y, which also wasn't intended. Just thought I'd try to add a perspective to cool some of the outrage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:34:48-07:00","id":981025,"title":"","content":"Honestly if the technocracy lost, it would lead to billions of death, society is so dependant on technology. So yeah, the technocracy methods might be abhorrant at times, but aside from the Sons of Ether maybe, they were dealing with people who didn't care avout the consquences of their actions.<br /> <br /> It'd be different if they were interested in a reasonable compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:51:48-07:00","id":981039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980923#post980923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the core idea behind the initial formation of the Technocracy, that magic should be made universally accessible rather than being left in the hands of the Enlightened elite to use or abuse as they saw fit, as really interesting given the metaphysics of Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is in fact their founding ethos that was eight centuries ago, and the Technocracy is not the Order of Reason. The Technocracy is exactly that: keeping magic and advanced technology in the hands of an enlightened elite and only handing it down from Olympus at a carefully controlled pace they have determined in their infallible wisdom. They talk a good game about humanity not being &quot;ready&quot; but that doesn't change the fact that the current order of things conveniently keep the Technocracy in charge, and that as long as they maintain control over the advancement of technology they'll always <i>be</i> in charge. They fear Ascension because they fear what humanity will do to them if they know everything the Technocracy has done and actually have the means to fight back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:07:03-07:00","id":981084,"title":"","content":"I don't understand how you all can be so upset by Shane's comment and treatment of Chronicles then turn around and throw the exact same types of comments x 10 at not only WoD but Gen X'ers as well.<br /> <br /> That said, I do agree it was not the best comment to make. Thankfully, I felt he handled the rest of the Q &amp; A very well, especially considering the nature of most questions. Also, it's good to remember he was instrumental in one main area: WoD Larp, and thus, has a very distanced view of not only Chronicles but WoD tabletop. I felt the Q &amp; A went well overall, and much was covered for the short time allotted and the wasted time on covering similar ground or questions that needed more time to answer than they had.<br /> <br /> I think I also remember mention of gambling pachinko machines advertising similar to Capcom, which seems like a waste of time/money. However, the older interview did really feel like a slap in the face to Chronicles, and also it feels very questionable to me that they are not only deadset on the metaplot without iterating to test it first, but are insistent on moving the prime location of WoD to their HQ. I don't mind it being darker and tackling real world issues: that is rather exciting. What concerns me is the possibility of it becoming so centric around their Larp community and location that they forget the rest of the world and/or hamstring themselves with too much metaplot.<br /> <br /> That said, I do feel it is useful to at least update the setting to include world events and so on that impacted a lot of people. I also wonder how much is lost in translation since it seems like for the guys heading the company, english is a second language, and so maybe they aren't as eloquent verbally as the nuances of trying to develop this amazing ip in their heads. Anyways, point being, at least for now, it's anyones guess what happens with the new White Wolf, but at least they're leaving Onyx Path to do their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:38:28-07:00","id":981099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980533#post980533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people are definitely reading a lot into Dave's statement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What <i>was </i>his statement again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:55:23-07:00","id":981106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981099#post981099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What <i>was </i>his statement again?</div> </div> </div> </div>That people misinterpreted the Technocracy as more heroic and less brainwashed than intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:01:32-07:00","id":981110,"title":"","content":"Meh. He's entitled to his opinion. I don't really care until he starts trying to get White Wolf to reign in OPP's work on CoD. Until then, he can say, &quot;We did it better&quot; and I can reply &quot;Ravnos&quot; until the cows come home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:09:44-07:00","id":981113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981084#post981084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wonder how much is lost in translation since it seems like for the guys heading the company, english is a second language, and so maybe they aren't as eloquent verbally as the nuances of trying to develop this amazing ip in their heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering these views have been expressed consistently and at multiple times in multiple ways, I honestly doubt they're translation artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:16:29-07:00","id":981119,"title":"","content":"And the guy who made the comment that started this thread is an American.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:33:23-07:00","id":981128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981106#post981106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That people misinterpreted the Technocracy as more heroic and less brainwashed than intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. That is not a problem I have, after thinking about the Technocrats for a while. They don't really question their actions, do they?<br /> <br /> Problem is, neither do the Traditions, and they're supposed to be the good guys. I can see why people would prefer the Union over the Trads if they come off as equally dogmatic-far better the people who <i>ostensibly </i>pursue a program of universal magic that anyone can grasp, if they have the opportunity. And forgetting that, thanks to the fact that Technocrats are still morally stuck in the Victorian era, they really don't understand that &quot;everyone&quot; is not the same as &quot;rich first worlders&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's honestly why I prefer Awakening-the writers of that game seem pretty clear on what distinguishes the good guys from the bad, and never forgetting to write that in (although in the Pentacle vs Seer philosophical knife-fight, it's less self-knowledge vs self-righteousness than it is often misguided idealism vs, cynicism as an excuse for selfishness and moral laziness).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:46:33-07:00","id":981133,"title":"","content":"Couldn't help but think &quot;ah, Fuck these guys&quot; during that interview. I think Martin (is that the right spelling?) was right on point with a lot of it. Rather disliked the podium guy for the times he tried to pander to the crowd. <br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is dark and it tries to make a point. You're able to fight against injustices. If you don't like that, Talk about it with your storyteller or something, but don't lobby to have things you don't like about real society not included in the game that's given to everyone because it makes you personally uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> A lot of that interview was painful. I could go into detail about the literary merits have having a dark and shitty world and and exceptions undermines that, but that'd take a long time.<br /> You're entitled to ask your storyteller for a safe space with something, but You're not entitled to lobby the entire series for everyone in accordance to personal triggers. Lobbying like that is terrible for artistic vision/statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 10-03-2016, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:51:01-07:00","id":981139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981128#post981128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. That is not a problem I have, after thinking about the Technocrats for a while. They don't really question their actions, do they?<br /> <br /> Problem is, neither do the Traditions, and they're supposed to be the good guys. I can see why people would prefer the Union over the Trads if they come off as equally dogmatic-far better the people who <i>ostensibly </i>pursue a program of universal magic that anyone can grasp, if they have the opportunity. And forgetting that, thanks to the fact that Technocrats are still morally stuck in the Victorian era, they really don't understand that &amp;quot;everyone&amp;quot; is not the same as &amp;quot;rich first worlders&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> It's honestly why I prefer Awakening-the writers of that game seem pretty clear on what distinguishes the good guys from the bad, and never forgetting to write that in (although in the Pentacle vs Seer philosophical knife-fight, it's less self-knowledge vs self-righteousness than it is often misguided idealism vs, cynicism as an excuse for selfishness and moral laziness).</div> </div> </div> </div> I will say in CoD its much clearer who thr good guys are and the bad guys are, even if the good guys some times do really bad things and some of the bad guys have descent motivates or do some good things, even if for selfish reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> True Fae, Huntsmen, Seers, most Scalasti, Pure, Pandoreans, Strix, all clearly marked as assholes. Are they're shades of grey within that, yes, but as a group no one is likely to be saying are they really the bad guys.<br /> <br /> Admittedly more a battle between antiheroes vs. Villians, then bad guy vs. good guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:59:54-07:00","id":981147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981025#post981025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly if the technocracy lost, it would lead to billions of death, society is so dependant on technology. So yeah, the technocracy methods might be abhorrant at times, but aside from the Sons of Ether maybe, they were dealing with people who didn't care avout the consquences of their actions.<br /> <br /> It'd be different if they were interested in a reasonable compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, perhaps thay'd work to create a world with consistent scientific laws, but still allow for magic and the unknown to exist, hidden on the fringes of the world, the rabble remaining aware of them, but refusing to acknowledge them for their own sanity's sake.<br /> <br /> Wait a minute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:59:40-07:00","id":981185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981133#post981133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't help but think &quot;ah, Fuck these guys&quot; during that interview. I think Martin (is that the right spelling?) was right on point with a lot of it. Rather disliked the podium guy for the times he tried to pander to the crowd.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is dark and it tries to make a point. You're able to fight against injustices. If you don't like that, Talk about it with your storyteller or something, but don't lobby to have things you don't like about real society not included in the game that's given to everyone because it makes you personally uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> A lot of that interview was painful. I could go into detail about the literary merits have having a dark and shitty world and and exceptions undermines that, but that'd take a long time.<br /> You're entitled to ask your storyteller for a safe space with something, but You're not entitled to lobby the entire series for everyone in accordance to personal triggers. Lobbying like that is terrible for artistic vision/statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:00:23-07:00","id":981186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981113#post981113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering these views have been expressed consistently and at multiple times in multiple ways, I honestly doubt they're translation artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah you're probably right. Unfortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:07:29-07:00","id":981193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981133#post981133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't help but think &amp;quot;ah, Fuck these guys&amp;quot; during that interview. I think Martin (is that the right spelling?) was right on point with a lot of it. Rather disliked the podium guy for the times he tried to pander to the crowd. <br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is dark and it tries to make a point. You're able to fight against injustices. If you don't like that, Talk about it with your storyteller or something, but don't lobby to have things you don't like about real society not included in the game that's given to everyone because it makes you personally uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> A lot of that interview was painful. I could go into detail about the literary merits have having a dark and shitty world and and exceptions undermines that, but that'd take a long time.<br /> You're entitled to ask your storyteller for a safe space with something, but You're not entitled to lobby the entire series for everyone in accordance to personal triggers. Lobbying like that is terrible for artistic vision/statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have completely missed the point of the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T21:17:55-07:00","id":981256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981128#post981128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. That is not a problem I have, after thinking about the Technocrats for a while. They don't really question their actions, do they?<br /> <br /> Problem is, neither do the Traditions, and they're supposed to be the good guys. I can see why people would prefer the Union over the Trads if they come off as equally dogmatic-far better the people who <i>ostensibly </i>pursue a program of universal magic that anyone can grasp, if they have the opportunity. And forgetting that, thanks to the fact that Technocrats are still morally stuck in the Victorian era, they really don't understand that &quot;everyone&quot; is not the same as &quot;rich first worlders&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's honestly why I prefer Awakening-the writers of that game seem pretty clear on what distinguishes the good guys from the bad, and never forgetting to write that in (although in the Pentacle vs Seer philosophical knife-fight, it's less self-knowledge vs self-righteousness than it is often misguided idealism vs, cynicism as an excuse for selfishness and moral laziness).</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the context in which that statement was made, explaining why the Seers are so clearly in the wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T21:22:44-07:00","id":981258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981193#post981193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have completely missed the point of the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also another better thread in the Masquerade forum where people are talking about the particular aspect of the q&amp;a that is totally off topic for this thread. Would be nice if he took it elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T23:46:12-07:00","id":981293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980819#post980819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af<br /> <br /> That's what you get with Open Dev. The fans spoketh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, the principles of this statement are very mixed bag for me. I am very suspicious of fans and their ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T23:46:51-07:00","id":981294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980850#post980850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked 4e, but I love 5e because it feels like all the best parts combined, then refined with completely new ideas like bounded accucy and advantage.<br /> <br /> As for pathfinder, I find 5e to be way better, although I like Golarion as a setting and the novels.<br /> <br /> But 5e has elements I really like that aren't present in patheefinder/3.x<br /> <br /> Although I'm interested in they're new spun off Starfinder when it comes out.<br /> <br /> Anyway back to the OWOD vs. CoD brewhaha, that the CEO of White Wolf carelessly started started.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different strokes for different folks. it happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T23:48:57-07:00","id":981296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=980876#post980876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean liking the authoritarian political leaning of the organization? Or you mean endless flamewars and bad internet behavior?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or any number of other things, really.<br /> <br /> When I describe what happened with the Technocracy as a mess, one should reasonably assume I am actually describing it as a flaming mess.<br /> <br /> The Fallout of GttT is not one of my favorite topics, but it is one I am strongly opinionated on. It's also one where my opinion is probably of less value than, say, Dave's. In fact, I'll say very definitely it's of less value than Dave's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-04-2016, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:32:27-07:00","id":981312,"title":"","content":"I watched the hour-long Key Notes and then I watched the hour-long Q&amp;A session. And then I read the interview that was basically a response to the other two. In my mind there's nothing spectacular or special here. The guys, and gal, over at White Wolf Entertainment are trying really hard to separate themselves from Onyx Path Publishing. They need to aggressively establish that White Wolf Entertainment and Onyx Path Publishing are two completely different things, so that they can create their own company image without getting into a messy situation where WWE (wait that's already taken...WWEN?) is mixed with OPP. The whole thing was just straight up posturing for fans. Fan service in the simplest and most direct way that I can think of. They didn't have any products to show. They had some images to show. They didn't have a new direction that WWEN is taking. They had, what sounded to me like, recycled ideas from the past dragged to the present.<br /> <br /> From this perspective it makes perfect sense to have OPP change the name of their core products. There is no more New World of Darkness. There is just the Chronicles of Darkness. And then there's the One World of Darkness, which is different, because it's hearkening back to the Good Old Days, but update to the current era. Well, at least they will attempt to do that.<br /> <br /> OPP is clearly listed as a partner of WWEN. So, it's not like these people actively hate each other. Aside from the cringe-worthy SJW bs I saw nothing noteworthy during the entire Q&amp;A-session. And of course they have to pander to that demographic, because it seems to me that everyone over at WWEN needs to pander to every demographic. At least until they have established themselves as a comany. So, in my opinion the Q&amp;A-session was a horrid mess, but largely inconsequential and meaningless. They don't want to drive sales to OPP, even if they like OPP. Therefore, it makes no sense to start talking about OPP and its products in a WWEN marketing conference. I know that it's called the Grand Masquerade, and there's more to it than what I saw, but honestly what I saw was a half-baked marketing conference followed by a really messy Q&amp;A-session. Nothing noteworthy until they actually do something. WWEN is a new company that needs to create its own image, and it is using WW nostalgia to get it going. Whether or not that's going to work in the long-run I have no idea. It sounds like a good idea. However, the truth is in the products and right now they have nothing.<br /> <br /> What I really didn't like about the WWEN Key Notes presentation was the implication that these people are done writing RPG books. They have done their share, and now it is time to get some freelancers to write the new books. It seems to me that if you want to bring back the Good Old Days, then the most direct way to do it is to have the people who started this whole glorious World of Darkness return to writing. Except, it was repeatedly pointed out that they are not the right people to do the writing. And the writers are exactly the people who are going to make or break WWEN. I don't know how this is all going to work out, but it sounded a lot like &quot;we here at White Wolf Entertainment are going to concentrate on the bigger picture, and allow others to create the content that you want according to our rules and guidelines.&quot; Now that's something that I don't like.<br /> <br /> So, right now it seems to me that WWEN has an existing fanbase, which will have to wait for at least 18 months (probably more, would be my guess) for V V. And along the way WWEN will probably try to sell all kinds of other stuff to their fans. To me it sounded a lot like covering every possible market and filling it with WWEN products. Works in theory. The way I see it the more partners and different kinds of people you bring onboard the more different kinds of interpretations you are going to get. And I know that they talked about this &quot;bible&quot; for OWOD, which is going to be sent out to every affiliate and partner, so they can all play together nicely. It will be very interesting to see how all of that works out in real-life.<br /> <br /> Also, OPP is still publishing cWoD books. I wonder how that's going to work out in the future?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T02:00:10-07:00","id":981352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981312#post981312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how this is all going to work out, but it sounded a lot like &quot;we here at White Wolf Entertainment are going to concentrate on the bigger picture, and allow others to create the content that you want according to our rules and guidelines.&quot; Now that's something that I don't like.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you strip away the specifics of the phrasing though... that's pretty much how the modern RPG industry operates. That's what OPP does too. Most RPG publishers have an extremely small staff that run the &quot;big picture&quot; stuff and then shop out the vast majority of the writing to freelancers that follow OPP guidelines while creating content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T03:11:18-07:00","id":981369,"title":"","content":"Can we not bring up the &quot;SJW&quot; stuff in this thread? Like at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T03:14:02-07:00","id":981370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981352#post981352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you strip away the specifics of the phrasing though... that's pretty much how the modern RPG industry operates. That's what OPP does too. Most RPG publishers have an extremely small staff that run the &quot;big picture&quot; stuff and then shop out the vast majority of the writing to freelancers that follow OPP guidelines while creating content.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm...I suppose so. My main concern is probably with &quot;who are they going to choose?&quot;, which is probably going to be answered with &quot;really good writers that they already know&quot;. I suppose my main worry is that this is going to create more competition for the writers available for such projects. For...12?...years it has just been the remnants of WW and OPP. Now we have another company that is doing almost exactly the same kind of product. Question is: who gets the good writer and for how long?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T03:17:58-07:00","id":981371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981312#post981312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it sounded a lot like covering every possible market and filling it with WWEN products. Works in theory. </div> </div> </div> </div>Im the only one who thinks this when reading the WW is convering every possible market for its products?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Beckett-Vampire-the-Masquerade-Figure/dp/B000GTN8NQ/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1475575929&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=Vampire+the+Masquerade+Figure\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Beckett-Vampire-the-Masquerade-Figure/dp/B000GTN8NQ/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1475575929&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=Vampire+the+Masquerade+Figure\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Beckett-Vampire-the-Masquerade-Figure/dp/B000GTN8NQ/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1475575929&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=Vampire+the+Masquerade+Figure\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/Beckett-Vampire-the-Masquerade-Figure/dp/B000GTN8NQ/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1475575929&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=Vampire+the+Masquerade+Figure </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We never got an anatole action figure. Move his arm for him to quote the bibble!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T06:56:17-07:00","id":981416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981369#post981369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we not bring up the &quot;SJW&quot; stuff in this thread? Like at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Social context is important, everything is politics. It kind of happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:18:33-07:00","id":981423,"title":"","content":"My biggest issue, I think, is the whole Werewolves versus Vampires trope again. Can't that just die out and stop painting entire groups of people with the same brush? Ugggghhhhh....<br /> <br /> Putting aside the social issue aspects of the Darkness games, my big priority when looking at these games are &quot;something new.&quot; I'm <b><i><u>bored</u> </i></b>with the same old stories repeated ad nausium. Vampires are corporate sharks and werewolves are grand soldiers at war. Something new please!<br /> <br /> Generalities being what they are, I'm going to wait to see the actual books before making a final judgement. But I'm hoping its really not going back that way.<br /> <br /> Yeah, there's the whole OneWoD v. CofD things going on, but that's no different than pretty much every culture in existance. Conservative versus new, globilization versus nationalism... we need a balance of these things, but its not very clear if we'll ever find them, let alone in a fan base for a game. So, I'm going to stick with just worrying abotu me and my group on game issues. I'll check out the books once they come out, I'll hope for a well done video game, but that's it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, as per D&amp;D 3.5 v. 4e v. 5e - one thing I do love on 5e is the attempt to put more effort into interaction and exploration over just combat. I love that they're trying. There needs to be a whole lot more done in that direction, but hopefully its a start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-04-2016, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T09:06:18-07:00","id":981474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981416#post981416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social context is important, everything is politics. It kind of happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's nice but I don't want this thread mired in comments like the one I reacted to. It was completely unnecessary and irrelevant to the thread topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:50:56-07:00","id":981528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981312#post981312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I watched the hour-long Key Notes and then I watched the hour-long Q&amp;A session. And then I read the interview that was basically a response to the other two. In my mind there's nothing spectacular or special here. The guys, and gal, over at White Wolf Entertainment are trying really hard to separate themselves from Onyx Path Publishing. They need to aggressively establish that White Wolf Entertainment and Onyx Path Publishing are two completely different things, so that they can create their own company image without getting into a messy situation where WWE (wait that's already taken...WWEN?) is mixed with OPP. The whole thing was just straight up posturing for fans. Fan service in the simplest and most direct way that I can think of. They didn't have any products to show. They had some images to show. They didn't have a new direction that WWEN is taking. They had, what sounded to me like, recycled ideas from the past dragged to the present.<br /> <br /> From this perspective it makes perfect sense to have OPP change the name of their core products. There is no more New World of Darkness. There is just the Chronicles of Darkness. And then there's the One World of Darkness, which is different, because it's hearkening back to the Good Old Days, but update to the current era. Well, at least they will attempt to do that.<br /> <br /> OPP is clearly listed as a partner of WWEN. So, it's not like these people actively hate each other. Aside from the cringe-worthy SJW bs I saw nothing noteworthy during the entire Q&amp;A-session. And of course they have to pander to that demographic, because it seems to me that everyone over at WWEN needs to pander to every demographic. At least until they have established themselves as a comany. So, in my opinion the Q&amp;A-session was a horrid mess, but largely inconsequential and meaningless. They don't want to drive sales to OPP, even if they like OPP. Therefore, it makes no sense to start talking about OPP and its products in a WWEN marketing conference. I know that it's called the Grand Masquerade, and there's more to it than what I saw, but honestly what I saw was a half-baked marketing conference followed by a really messy Q&amp;A-session. Nothing noteworthy until they actually do something. WWEN is a new company that needs to create its own image, and it is using WW nostalgia to get it going. Whether or not that's going to work in the long-run I have no idea. It sounds like a good idea. However, the truth is in the products and right now they have nothing.<br /> <br /> What I really didn't like about the WWEN Key Notes presentation was the implication that these people are done writing RPG books. They have done their share, and now it is time to get some freelancers to write the new books. It seems to me that if you want to bring back the Good Old Days, then the most direct way to do it is to have the people who started this whole glorious World of Darkness return to writing. Except, it was repeatedly pointed out that they are not the right people to do the writing. And the writers are exactly the people who are going to make or break WWEN. I don't know how this is all going to work out, but it sounded a lot like &amp;quot;we here at White Wolf Entertainment are going to concentrate on the bigger picture, and allow others to create the content that you want according to our rules and guidelines.&amp;quot; Now that's something that I don't like.<br /> <br /> So, right now it seems to me that WWEN has an existing fanbase, which will have to wait for at least 18 months (probably more, would be my guess) for V V. And along the way WWEN will probably try to sell all kinds of other stuff to their fans. To me it sounded a lot like covering every possible market and filling it with WWEN products. Works in theory. The way I see it the more partners and different kinds of people you bring onboard the more different kinds of interpretations you are going to get. And I know that they talked about this &amp;quot;bible&amp;quot; for OWOD, which is going to be sent out to every affiliate and partner, so they can all play together nicely. It will be very interesting to see how all of that works out in real-life.<br /> <br /> Also, OPP is still publishing cWoD books. I wonder how that's going to work out in the future?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well said, all of it, well said. WWEN is way too cocky for a company that has directly produced nothing, but a trailer and an extra layer of bureacracy for Onyx Path, the people actually making stuff to deal with.<br /> <br /> Abd yeah that Q&amp;A was an absolute mess, bit to be fair the lions share of that belongs to the podium guy and an audience that behaved poorly for the most part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:51:47-07:00","id":981530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981474#post981474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's nice but I don't want this thread mired in comments like the one I reacted to. It was completely unnecessary and irrelevant to the thread topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason it was brought up is that it monopolized 2/3 of the entire Q &amp; A. It's not like it's some random one question, literally most of the time was wasted on that. Else, IMHO the Q &amp; A might've gone much better with more pertinent, relevant questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:55:27-07:00","id":981531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981133#post981133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't help but think &quot;ah, Fuck these guys&quot; during that interview. I think Martin (is that the right spelling?) was right on point with a lot of it. Rather disliked the podium guy for the times he tried to pander to the crowd. <br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is dark and it tries to make a point. You're able to fight against injustices. If you don't like that, Talk about it with your storyteller or something, but don't lobby to have things you don't like about real society not included in the game that's given to everyone because it makes you personally uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> A lot of that interview was painful. I could go into detail about the literary merits have having a dark and shitty world and and exceptions undermines that, but that'd take a long time.<br /> You're entitled to ask your storyteller for a safe space with something, but You're not entitled to lobby the entire series for everyone in accordance to personal triggers. Lobbying like that is terrible for artistic vision/statement.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought podium guy was Martin, and pony tail guy was Shane?<br /> <br /> I don't know. I agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-04-2016, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:01:21-07:00","id":981535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981530#post981530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason it was brought up is that it monopolized 2/3 of the entire Q &amp; A. It's not like it's some random one question, literally most of the time was wasted on that. Else, IMHO the Q &amp; A might've gone much better with more pertinent, relevant questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo!<br /> <br /> As for other Q&amp;A thread, I can't find it in the OWOD forum section of this site.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:14:59-07:00","id":981545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981530#post981530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason it was brought up is that it monopolized 2/3 of the entire Q &amp; A. It's not like it's some random one question, literally most of the time was wasted on that. Else, IMHO the Q &amp; A might've gone much better with more pertinent, relevant questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The time wasn't wasted on any of it. These are things modern media companies should be concerned about. I'm sorry you think respectful representation is a waste of time but your thoughts on this are literally irrelevant since you wrongly think it is a waste of time. However, not important to you does not mean not important at all, and you probably need to realize the world is bigger than your personal needs. Now can we drop this digression and never mention it again in this thread because it is off-topic? The actual subject here is what WW has to say about CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:17:46-07:00","id":981547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981530#post981530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason it was brought up is that it monopolized 2/3 of the entire Q &amp; A. It's not like it's some random one question, literally most of the time was wasted on that. Else, IMHO the Q &amp; A might've gone much better with more pertinent, relevant questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So go talk about it in a thread where the subject is the Q&amp;A as a whole. Or start your own if you can't find one. <i>This thread</i>, being in the Chronicles of Darkness forum, has been about the answers specifically related to Chronicles of Darkness, until a sockpuppet account for a banned user showed up and posted a non-sequitur rant about political correctness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981535#post981535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bingo!<br /> <br /> As for other Q&amp;A thread, I can't find it in the OWOD forum section of this site.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've been discussing it in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/963352-vampire-tm-5th-edition?p=977986#post977986\">this thread</a> since the Q&amp;A went up. And anyway, if you can't find a thread for a topic you want to discuss, you should start one instead of derailing another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:18:00-07:00","id":981600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981370#post981370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm...I suppose so. My main concern is probably with &quot;who are they going to choose?&quot;, which is probably going to be answered with &quot;really good writers that they already know&quot;. I suppose my main worry is that this is going to create more competition for the writers available for such projects. For...12?...years it has just been the remnants of WW and OPP. Now we have another company that is doing almost exactly the same kind of product. Question is: who gets the good writer and for how long?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that is explicitly not that answer that they gave. WW has been incredibly consistent and clear that they want to put energy into finding new writers instead of sticking with the old hands.<br /> <br /> As well, OPP has been pretty good at recruitment. A significant portion of the current mainstay OPP freelancers were picked out from the community rather than from the remnants of WW/CCP.<br /> <br /> So sure, there's going to be some competition (there already is, even if it isn't between partner companies), but with OPP and WW both looking engaged in efforts to expand their go-to writers I don't see this as an issue that will lead to problems for the CofD. Esp. with the freelance model since nobody freelancing for OPP on the CofD is obligated to move to work on WW projects because WW needs some extra writers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981423#post981423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest issue, I think, is the whole Werewolves versus Vampires trope again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? They're doing the WoD, that's a thing in the WoD. Since there's been no comment about wanting it to move beyond what's already in that universe, I'm not sure what the concern is. It's not like they said anything about making the CofD more like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981531#post981531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought podium guy was Martin, and pony tail guy was Shane?</div> </div> </div> </div>Other way around. If it helps at all, Martin is also the guy that's on the left side of the background image of this website from his modelling for the V20 Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:06:18-07:00","id":981681,"title":"","content":"I used to larp with Shane back in the Camarilla days. This is one reason his comments made me sad. I mean not that we were friends or anything. Different circles/cliques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:54:17-07:00","id":981707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981545#post981545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The time wasn't wasted on any of it. These are things modern media companies should be concerned about. I'm sorry you think respectful representation is a waste of time but your thoughts on this are literally irrelevant since you wrongly think it is a waste of time. However, not important to you does not mean not important at all, and you probably need to realize the world is bigger than your personal needs. Now can we drop this digression and never mention it again in this thread because it is off-topic? The actual subject here is what WW has to say about CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div> The questions were extremely repetitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:55:55-07:00","id":981708,"title":"","content":"That's nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:59:06-07:00","id":981710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981547#post981547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So go talk about it in a thread where the subject is the Q&amp;A as a whole. Or start your own if you can't find one. <i>This thread</i>, being in the Chronicles of Darkness forum, has been about the answers specifically related to Chronicles of Darkness, until a sockpuppet account for a banned user showed up and posted a non-sequitur rant about political correctness.<br /> <br /> <br /> They've been discussing it in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/963352-vampire-tm-5th-edition?p=977986#post977986&amp;quot;]this</a> thread[/URL] since the Q&amp;A went up. And anyway, if you can't find a thread for a topic you want to discuss, you should start one instead of derailing another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for the link.<br /> <br /> Anyways back to the WWEN bashing of CoD, I think its a fundlement betrayal of Onyx Path and disrespectful of a business partner given that CoD is bssically Onyx Paths center piece line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","na