s-up?p=981763#post981763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always had the notion that they will keep Chronicles around until they need some quick cash and spin the property off to some third party. This doesn't alleviate my concerns</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully OPP could be that third party? Happened with Scion and Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:46:28-07:00","id":981792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981761#post981761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mhmm, it definitely seems like they're trying to have it both ways. Bash on Chronicles to win over the nWoD haters, while simultaneously cashing in on the license. And to be fair, better that than to discontinue Chronicles, but it doesn't do anything to endear me to them or want to support their One World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Exactly my feelings on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:49:09-07:00","id":981794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981788#post981788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hopefully OPP could be that third party? Happened with Scion and Aberrant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would honestly hope it would be them but it would probably be who could ever afford the price tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:58:48-07:00","id":981802,"title":"","content":"It certainly seems like the White-Wolf and the WoD has become a hot patoato for gaming companies lately. <br /> <br /> Though, to be honest? Its not like there are a lot of urban fantasy / horror style games out there, so there will always be a niche for the CofD. Even if it has to be rebranded under a different name. Its not like anyone can copyright the idea of vampires, werewolves and witches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:29:47-07:00","id":981880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981794#post981794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would honestly hope it would be them but it would probably be who could ever afford the price tag.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think CoD is endanger, because I don't see WWEN having enough respect for CoD to concider it a threat. So CoD with continue as it is under the radar.<br /> <br /> Plus CoD has nearly zero expenses, only profits in budget reports, which looks good to the bean counters, to them its free profits from a line they don't care about.<br /> <br /> So there can be an advantage to being over looked by the powerful, more room freedom.<br /> <br /> Personal I love CoD, its tied with Startrek, Stargate, and the Forgotten Realms as my favourite setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:32:33-07:00","id":981884,"title":"","content":"I didn't say they were planning on spinning it off anytime soon, only that they might if the need or opportunity arises. After all having your own off brand is kinda weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:32:43-07:00","id":981885,"title":"","content":"I think for me, part of my current reservations about the WoD revival, and my irritation about Shane's comments (and I know, I know, it's probably a PR move and an appeal to the core fanbase) is that the WoD was so important and formative in my adolescence. Like a lot of things tinged with nostalgia, that leaves it sort of trapped in amber.<br /> <br /> I found a copy of the Vampire: The Masquerade core book (1st edition, I believe) in my best friend's older brother's room. I was in fifth grade, right in that transitional phase between being a child and growing into a teenager. And frankly, the jagged drawings and devil-may-care demeanor seemed so transgressive to me. I was familiar and briefly intrigued with Dungeons and Dragons, and I loved the potential there, but my flirtation with traditional fantasy was brief, and the crunchiness of the rules was just too much for me to overcome. Elves and dwarves and superheroes seemed like kiddie stuff to me. The whole DnD Satanism scare was still bubbling in the background (and I grew up to a fairly progressive family in the South), but this was the first thing that seemed edgy to me. It seemed dangerous. It was my first exposure to fantasy-horror, and it went hand in hand with my discovery of punk music. It was something to spark my creative instincts without seeming too dorky. In retrospect, a lot of the world building was cheesy, but I gobbled up every piece of it, and I think for a lot of kids my age, it hit all the right notes in their teenage angst. Really looking at it, it's the same sort of world building you see in a high fantasy or sci-fi setting, but that fusion of the modern world with fantasy and the attitude of the writers (along with katanas and manwolves and trenchcoats) just seemed like the epitome of cool to me, and I think it served as a sort of anchoring element for a lot of kids figuring themselves out. I remember talking about these games with gutter punks and theater kids and bohemian kids. I remember playing a game of Werewolf with an older group of stoner skaters. It was the perfect place and the perfect time, and it intersected with everything that seemed cool to a 14/15/16 year old kid growing up in the early 90s. It seemed like it was saying something important, and my memories of friendships, first girlfriends, and music are all tangled up in the game. Eventually I moved on to other things, and my memory of the cWoD is still heavily shaded with those feelings of nostalgia. I can look back at it now and see the things that seem either dated or just outright cheesy, but it's something that always brings about a tingly feeling in my heart. I'm curious to know if people who grew up on Chronicles feel the same way. It doesn't seem like it's as firmly rooted in the zeitgeist of its time, but then, I wasn't a growing boy in that time, so I can't especially say.<br /> <br /> So that's the perspective I come from when I hear these guys talk. It's just that nothing they've announced seems to reflect the desire to capture the die hard fans who have stayed with the game for decades (not that there's anything wrong with that), but those comments seem so insulting to the writers and editors who spent over a decade developing these games. I remember flipping through a few of these books a year or two after the CoD was launched. It didn't do much for me then. But now I'm in my early 30s now. ChroD doesn't grip me the way that WoD did then, but that's fine. Hell, you don't feel anything as strongly as you did when you're an angry, horny, impressionable teen. And ChroD is exactly what I want. I don't doubt it wouldn't exist without WoD blazing the trail, but in so many ways, it's developed on those core storytelling values in a natural and organic way. I like my stories leaner and with more player agency now, but I don't deride people who feel differently about it. And I just worry about how well, in the long term, ChroD will stay afloat. In the hypothetical situation where WoD becomes a worldwide phenomena, will the higher ups decide that OPP's games are diluting the brand? Or will they try to fold it back into their corporate umbrella?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:23:57-07:00","id":981907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981884#post981884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say they were planning on spinning it off anytime soon, only that they might if the need or opportunity arises. After all having your own off brand is kinda weird.</div> </div> </div> </div> To the WWEN CoD doesn't rate off brand status, but v20 might, so I feel bad for v20 fans. I mean doing WoD 5th edition so soon on the heels of v20 does not bode well for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:36:55-07:00","id":981912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981907#post981907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To the WWEN CoD doesn't rate off brand status, but v20 might, so I feel bad for v20 fans. I mean doing WoD 5th edition so soon on the heels of v20 does not bode well for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 came out how long ago again? 5 years? It's purely a nostalgia brand and 5th ed won't be out till what 2018 at best and even then it's a core book with maybe a St or players book less then a year later. By then all the V20 stuff would have already been out. What's left the Jihad diary? Maybe a V20 Chicago by night if the interest is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:39:17-07:00","id":981954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979103#post979103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, absolutely. And to their credit, WoD is absolutely the better choice for a multimedia brand. The WoD metaplot lends itself to a setting bible in a way the ChroD toolbox never could, and the only way I could see a ChroD TV show working is as something like American Horror Story where each season is a self-contained story starring the same actors. But since American Horror Story already does that, it wouldn't be as marketable to a network. Like, everything they've been doing makes sense given their business plan, which is part of why I'm more inclined to believe that the consistent displays of negativity towards ChroD is calculated. If they actually disliked ChroD, they could have killed it (as Martin was so keen to point out), but they didn't. I doubt they have any beef with ChroD, they just know their target audience likes when they talk shit about it. Which is obnoxious, but as long as they leave ChroD alone otherwise, I can shrug off their distasteful comments about it and keep playing my games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> resing the 2nd page... lol. So I think you could do a different kind of ChroD TV Show, or rather I think you could do ChroD like you Marvel and DC, the world is too broad for one show, and in fact doesn't even require a cohesive plot imo. Simply put you could allow many producers of ChroD TV shows, with many inter or unrelated story lines. where as WoD requires a more cohesive storyline that is more intertwined.<br /> <br /> To me ChroD is a &quot;Universe&quot;, WoD is a Story.<br /> <br /> Also I agree with you, I wish they would stop badmouthing chrod. It feels crappy to be dissing the people who are still moving things forward for them. Maybe we'll get lucky and they'll sell ChroD to OPP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:56:03-07:00","id":981958,"title":"","content":"'nother thing I want to say. I wish that we could stop talking about what nWoD was in relation to what cWoD was, I'm more interested in what ChroD is. I think one of the defining problems, imho, of nWoD is that it was too reminiscent of cWoD, but had problems defining its own personality (it felt like windows Me to 98 (at least Vampire does, imo)), whereas 2e I feel truly is able to stand on its own, to me the 2e world seems much more unique. That's not to put down 1e nWoD, but I don't feel like this God Machine run world, where shadow owls strike, and living nightmares stalk you, is a shadow of the masquerade (and whatever).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T22:07:15-07:00","id":981962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981958#post981958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'nother thing I want to say. I wish that we could stop talking about what nWoD was in relation to what cWoD was, I'm more interested in what ChroD is. I think one of the defining problems, imho, of nWoD is that it was too reminiscent of cWoD, but had problems defining its own personality (it felt like windows Me to 98 (at least Vampire does, imo)), whereas 2e I feel truly is able to stand on its own, to me the 2e world seems much more unique. That's not to put down 1e nWoD, but I don't feel like this God Machine run world, where shadow owls strike, and living nightmares stalk you, is a shadow of the masquerade (and whatever).</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta agree with you here. The 1E stuff largely felt like cWoD with the serial numbers filed off. That's not necessarily a bad thing. It seemed pretty clear that they wanted to take the core principles of the WoD and avoid the snarls that came from a stacking continuity, but that also meant that it was missing a lot of character. That's not a knock to the teams behind those books. Any new experiment takes some time to figure out. But I don't think the core games hit their stride until after Mage. Ever since Promethean, the lines have been very unique, and with 2E, they've been knocking all the books out of the park. I'd go so far as to say that the new ChroD really only resembles cWoD insofar as they're both urban horror fantasies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T02:01:01-07:00","id":982019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981958#post981958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'nother thing I want to say. I wish that we could stop talking about what nWoD was in relation to what cWoD was, I'm more interested in what ChroD is. I think one of the defining problems, imho, of nWoD is that it was too reminiscent of cWoD, but had problems defining its own personality (it felt like windows Me to 98 (at least Vampire does, imo)), whereas 2e I feel truly is able to stand on its own, to me the 2e world seems much more unique. That's not to put down 1e nWoD, but I don't feel like this God Machine run world, where shadow owls strike, and living nightmares stalk you, is a shadow of the masquerade (and whatever).</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who was never able to invest <i>anything</i> into cWoD, I also wish this very, very badly, but it's pretty hard when a large proportion of the talkative fans of CofD happen to be old hands at cWoD as well.<br /> <br /> I feel confident introducing new people directly to CofD (we're anxiously awaiting C:tL 2e at the moment, me especially because there are hacks I can't suss out until I have more information), but I also feel compelled to preface my introductions with, &quot;Also, there's this other set of gamelines that's superficially similar and, if you go on the internet, you'll basically find a ton of edition wars,&quot; just so that my inductees aren't blindsided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T02:21:13-07:00","id":982024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981547#post981547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So go talk about it in a thread where the subject is the Q&amp;A as a whole. Or start your own if you can't find one. <i>This thread</i>, being in the Chronicles of Darkness forum, has been about the answers specifically related to Chronicles of Darkness, until a sockpuppet account for a banned user showed up and posted a non-sequitur rant about political correctness.<br /> <br /> <br /> They've been discussing it in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/963352-vampire-tm-5th-edition?p=977986#post977986\">this thread</a> since the Q&amp;A went up. And anyway, if you can't find a thread for a topic you want to discuss, you should start one instead of derailing another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread is titled So the WW Q &amp; A is up, not something more specific like Q &amp; A and the future of White Wolf. You're really accusing me of derailing the thread? All I did was mention it once. Then someone else did, then another person jumped down their throat, then another person jumped down mine for mentioning it. Now you say this. Logic of all this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T02:23:42-07:00","id":982025,"title":"","content":"I gave my overall thoughts on the Q &amp; A, which included a brief mention of that topic. I'm not a mind reader, and I wasn't aware of a specific thread on that topic, but even if I were, are you saying it's forbidden to even mention it here? That doesn't make any sense. Preventing flame wars, sure, a noble goal. I did not incite anything of that nature, by stating an opinion. All I did was give my take on it, which is, unless I'm mistaken, the whole point of this thread. If that's not explanation enough, I don't know what will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","user":"zeroninja","date":".  Clarification. 10-05-2016, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T03:18:26-07:00","id":982039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up#post978952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right here: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8fhpXrrLBsI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8fhpXrrLBsI</a><br /> <br /> About 20 minutes in, there's a question about the old vs. new World of Darkness. Shane DeFreest makes a comment to the effect that the World of Darkness was designed as a world first and then a game, but that the Chronicles of Darkness was designed as a game first, and that this is a flaw. I'm not sure what to think wrt that, given that I generally like ChroD versions of games more than CWoD versions. Martin Ericsson's response is a bit kinder to ChroD.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to pick an argument or anything here, but I am wondering what people think about the commentary.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect to Shane, the facts, in terms of the design history at work, are the opposite. The classic WoD games were planned by name, but were designed sequentially, including their core setting concepts. Like, when VtM was released Mage's Consensus was not a thing. Changeling wasn't even the name of the game and had no core concept. By Revised the editorial line was to put the line you were working on before the idea of a cohesive setting. 2nd tried for heavy integration with mixed results.<br /> <br /> CofD was designed to support integrated games in a common setting from the beginning, right down to discussions about how different types of characters interacted socially and supernaturally.<br /> <br /> However! To be fair the solution for CofD was to amp up the level of mystery, the number of unanswered questions, and to take a light touch, so those efforts were invisible. The funny thing is that when, say, Mage: The Ascension says something about the CWoD setting and Werewolf contradicts it you end up with a lot of loud interactions because fans get on about it and creators have to deal with it. When the problem comes solved out the gate, it doesn't draw as much attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T03:40:30-07:00","id":982044,"title":"","content":"Anyway, having worked on WoD material back in the old White Wolf as well as what is now called CofD, I suppose my main insight is that the process of keeping the WoD going for over a decade the first time around imparted a number of lessons and insights that I cajoled and inferred out of people I worked with, and which I learned directly, myself. I'll be interested to see how many of those lessons were learned by other people. There's a tendency in game design on established lines for folks to come in and decide their predecessors didn't know a damn thing and they're totally going to fix everything. Then they make the same mistakes. (Incidentally, Storypath, which I designed the mechanical spine of, is meant to be specifically hardened against this problem.) I think this is probably inevitable and even part of the creative process, but it still means you can expect a rough ride as the team finds its feet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 10-05-2016, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T03:48:25-07:00","id":982046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982039#post982039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With all due respect to Shane, the facts, in terms of the design history at work, are the opposite. The classic WoD games were planned by name, but were designed sequentially, including their core setting concepts. Like, when VtM was released Mage's Consensus was not a thing. Changeling wasn't even the name of the game and had no core concept. By Revised the editorial line was to put the line you were working on before the idea of a cohesive setting. 2nd tried for heavy integration with mixed results.<br /> <br /> CofD was designed to support integrated games in a common setting from the beginning, right down to discussions about how different types of characters interacted socially and supernaturally.<br /> <br /> However! To be fair the solution for CofD was to amp up the level of mystery, the number of unanswered questions, and to take a light touch, so those efforts were invisible. The funny thing is that when, say, Mage: The Ascension says something about the CWoD setting and Werewolf contradicts it you end up with a lot of loud interactions because fans get on about it and creators have to deal with it. When the problem comes solved out the gate, it doesn't draw as much attention.</div> </div> </div> </div> Facinating, that thank you for the design comparison and the rebuttle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T03:56:51-07:00","id":982048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981954#post981954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> resing the 2nd page... lol. So I think you could do a different kind of ChroD TV Show, or rather I think you could do ChroD like you Marvel and DC, the world is too broad for one show, and in fact doesn't even require a cohesive plot imo. Simply put you could allow many producers of ChroD TV shows, with many inter or unrelated story lines. where as WoD requires a more cohesive storyline that is more intertwined.<br /> <br /> To me ChroD is a &amp;quot;Universe&amp;quot;, WoD is a Story.<br /> <br /> Also I agree with you, I wish they would stop badmouthing chrod. It feels crappy to be dissing the people who are still moving things forward for them. Maybe we'll get lucky and they'll sell ChroD to OPP.</div> </div> </div> </div> So as an analogy, WoD is Dragonlance to CoDs Forgotten Realms.<br /> <br /> I could see a more traditional show in CoD easily, especially using 2e, you focus on using the regional settings like Honshu/Tokyo, Toronto, Seattle, the Rockies, Miami, Montreal, Paris, Hong Kong, Baghdad, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T04:21:25-07:00","id":982053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982046#post982046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Facinating, that thank you for the design comparison and the rebuttle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm sure Shane has more complex thoughts than that quip. One if the interesting things about the WoD is that it's design was pretty jazzy, in that folks fluidly solved problems with whatever was on hand instead of building things off of a strict structure. Like, the Brujah add their lore and setting beats to VtM but they were also, intentionally, totally a way to play a Fighter-type character. That gives it an organic feeling that adds to immersion, so a &quot;game&quot; solution also contributes something to the world. The fact that WoD systems and concepts are designed to address action in the world means that even after all this time I can still design WoD stuff about twice as fast as CofD stuff, as I learned working on some Mage and Vampire books after maybe a decade away from that setting. So even though I don't agree with the account of how this stuff was made, I do see it as more of a statement of focus -- though again, I'd say that work like the Seers of the Throne really was about the world, not just clockwork for the game machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T04:45:56-07:00","id":982058,"title":"","content":"&quot;The fact that WoD systems and concepts are designed to address action in the world means that even after all this time I can still design WoD stuff about twice as fast as CofD stuff, as I learned working on some Mage and Vampire&quot;<br /> <br /> Why does CoD stuff take longer to design then WoD stuff, like what are CoD's systems and concepts designed to address in comparison?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T06:05:29-07:00","id":982085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982044#post982044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, having worked on WoD material back in the old White Wolf as well as what is now called CofD, I suppose my main insight is that the process of keeping the WoD going for over a decade the first time around imparted a number of lessons and insights that I cajoled and inferred out of people I worked with, and which I learned directly, myself. I'll be interested to see how many of those lessons were learned by other people. There's a tendency in game design on established lines for folks to come in and decide their predecessors didn't know a damn thing and they're totally going to fix everything. Then they make the same mistakes. (Incidentally, Storypath, which I designed the mechanical spine of, is meant to be specifically hardened against this problem.) I think this is probably inevitable and even part of the creative process, but it still means you can expect a rough ride as the team finds its feet.</div> </div> </div> </div>software devs do this too, I think probably all &quot;creators&quot; of large projects, do. Sometimes we're right to do it, and we all make mistakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T09:25:28-07:00","id":982168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=981545#post981545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The time wasn't wasted on any of it. These are things modern media companies should be concerned about. I'm sorry you think respectful representation is a waste of time but your thoughts on this are literally irrelevant since you wrongly think it is a waste of time. However, not important to you does not mean not important at all, and you probably need to realize the world is bigger than your personal needs. Now can we drop this digression and never mention it again in this thread because it is off-topic? The actual subject here is what WW has to say about CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are issues uniquely personal to one subset of fans. The arguments made by you here and on the video comments as well as the commentor who was brought up imply that not only does certain content need to be censored, but that one subset is &gt; all other fans and the company itself. Then you attack me for having an opinion that differs from that in the same way. So no, it seems you may be someone who needs to realize the future of White Wolf doesn't revolve around you specifically even if it's at the detriment of others. My original point on mentioning it wasn't that it didn't need to be brought up at all but that it didn't need to monopolize that much time and/or make demands of White Wolf that disregard their core philosophy. <br /> <br /> You are right about one thing though: WW's views are what's important on this matter in the end - not yours or mine specifically. Which is why I gave my overall views on the Q &amp; A. Just because something was brought up is not call for you to bash those with a differing opinion. I gave my overall views already. I also found it interesting to read all the comparisons to D &amp; D, although I've never played D &amp; D or even Pathfinder. It makes a lot of sense why ChroD is what it is considering the different areas WoD succeeded or fell short in.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:11:41-07:00","id":982182,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't understand why anyone feels the need to disparage WoD <i>or</i> ChroD in favor of the other. The two games, although similar, are trying to do very different things, and all things considered, they each do what they set out to do pretty well (neither does it perfectly, but that's just life). I mean, complaining that WoD is &quot;world first&quot; or complaining because ChroD is &quot;game first&quot; is like complaining because you can't cook your food with your lamp. That lamp was never meant to be used for cooking, and if you're trying and failing to cook with your lamp, that's not the lamp manufacturer's problem. Get a hot plate or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:30:02-07:00","id":982191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982168#post982168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are issues uniquely personal to one subset of fans. The arguments made by you here and on the video comments as well as the commentor who was brought up imply that not only does certain content need to be censored, but that one subset is &gt; all other fans and the company itself. Then you attack me for having an opinion that differs from that in the same way. So no, it seems you may be someone who needs to realize the future of White Wolf doesn't revolve around you specifically even if it's at the detriment of others. My original point on mentioning it wasn't that it didn't need to be brought up at all but that it didn't need to monopolize that much time and/or make demands of White Wolf that disregard their core philosophy.<br /> <br /> You are right about one thing though: WW's views are what's important on this matter in the end - not yours or mine specifically. Which is why I gave my overall views on the Q &amp; A. Just because something was brought up is not call for you to bash those with a differing opinion. I gave my overall views already. I also found it interesting to read all the comparisons to D &amp; D, although I've never played D &amp; D or even Pathfinder. It makes a lot of sense why ChroD is what it is considering the different areas WoD succeeded or fell short in.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just drop it. There's a thread in the CWoD Vampire forum (Charlaquin linked it earlier) where you can discuss this to your heart's content and I won't even go over there and tell y'all you're all wrong again.<br /> <br /> I didn't attack or bash anyone. Disagreement isn't an attack, it isn't bashing. Don't be so hypersensitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-05-2016, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:36:49-07:00","id":982231,"title":"","content":"I haven't watched the Q &amp; A yet but before I do something strikes me oddly. As a WoD vet it seems a pretty central aspect of the World of Darkness's tone is found in it's social commentary. Whether it's always executed well is a different story, but White Wolf games have always dove deeply into the concept. So I don't imagine that is going to change any time soon even with this new generation of White Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:31:47-07:00","id":982266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982191#post982191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just drop it. There's a thread in the CWoD Vampire forum (Charlaquin linked it earlier) where you can discuss this to your heart's content and I won't even go over there<b> and tell y'all you're all wrong again.</b><br /> <br /> I didn't attack or bash anyone. Disagreement isn't an attack, it isn't bashing. <b>Don't be so hypersensitive</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bThat is in fact bashing/attacking (and rudely dismissing) someone. You also repeatedly mentioned that their opinions and feelings were wrong/unimportant and they needed to realize this. I would suggest not telling people to &quot;Just drop it&quot; as well because that comes across as being unnecessarily antagonistic. If you have an issue with someone's post (in this case being &quot;off topic&quot;) report it and let the moderators deal with it it if we deem it necessary. No need for a confrontational reply to every post you disagree with.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:54:23-07:00","id":982441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982058#post982058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;The fact that WoD systems and concepts are designed to address action in the world means that even after all this time I can still design WoD stuff about twice as fast as CofD stuff, as I learned working on some Mage and Vampire&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Why does CoD stuff take longer to design then WoD stuff, like what are CoD's systems and concepts designed to address in comparison?</div> </div> </div> </div>In WoD you have many more switches to throw and less of an overarching game design mission. CofD has some specific principles you need to obey every time. Some folks forget, but this is generally the case. For instance, in WoD I can monkey with the target number, play with accumulated successes in a fine-grained manner, and use opposing dice pools in a freewheeling way. In CofD the target number is fixed in all but one game, opposed rolls are not as common because of the principle of keeping the number of dice rolls to a minimum, and there's a general desire to avoid best options for things, even if representing the world becomes less of a direct thing. So if I want to design, say, some rule for a flying kick, in WoD I just do it with whatever will produce a result that feels like it will output a flying kick in the world. In CofD I have a smaller set of tools and of course, model Merits to compare to.<br /> <br /> I don't think any one way is the best, but I will note that WoD comes from an era immediately after the &quot;realism&quot; focus of the 80s and In the infancy of the genre emulation trend, and when the idea was that rules were ways to describe how things work in the world with a dramatic edge, and that one would, when necessary, use them as benchmarks for streamlined and freed form play, and never as RAW. Contemporary game designers often don't understand or like these principles, and they don't work when you're not playing with a group that has built a high degree of mutual trust, so this has fallen by the wayside to the point where even though many fans get it and like it, you may never see these ideas embraced again. I think it deserves another look, but given that MET is basically anathema to this in its current form, where it is designed to moderate between antagonists in a PvP context, I'm not sure we'll see it from WW either. CofD is designed to be fast and stable, though it requires a level of abstraction that makes the semi-free form option trickier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T17:31:52-07:00","id":982459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982441#post982441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In WoD you have many more switches to throw and less of an overarching game design mission. CofD has some specific principles you need to obey every time. Some folks forget, but this is generally the case. For instance, in WoD I can monkey with the target number, play with accumulated successes in a fine-grained manner, and use opposing dice pools in a freewheeling way. In CofD the target number is fixed in all but one game, opposed rolls are not as common because of the principle of keeping the number of dice rolls to a minimum, and there's a general desire to avoid best options for things, even if representing the world becomes less of a direct thing. So if I want to design, say, some rule for a flying kick, in WoD I just do it with whatever will produce a result that feels like it will output a flying kick in the world. In CofD I have a smaller set of tools and of course, model Merits to compare to.<br /> <br /> I don't think any one way is the best, but I will note that WoD comes from an era immediately after the &quot;realism&quot; focus of the 80s and In the infancy of the genre emulation trend, and when the idea was that rules were ways to describe how things work in the world with a dramatic edge, and that one would, when necessary, use them as benchmarks for streamlined and freed form play, and never as RAW. Contemporary game designers often don't understand or like these principles, and they don't work when you're not playing with a group that has built a high degree of mutual trust, so this has fallen by the wayside to the point where even though many fans get it and like it, you may never see these ideas embraced again. I think it deserves another look, but given that MET is basically anathema to this in its current form, where it is designed to moderate between antagonists in a PvP context, I'm not sure we'll see it from WW either. CofD is designed to be fast and stable, though it requires a level of abstraction that makes the semi-free form option trickier.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, it's the the price of having to Optimize the game mechanics before hand so that the players don't need to spend time jury rigging later?<br /> I'll admit, I just thought it was due to the eras being different, but I didn't realize the gulf in mechanical setup had that result. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T07:46:46-07:00","id":982687,"title":"","content":"Ok. I apologize for my earlier comment. I think I was quite heated that day.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think they're right to criticise NWoD for it's neutrality, but at the same time, They could really criticise oWoD for it's plot, because oWoD is nothing if not inconsistent. The strength of not building yourself around a consistent world is, well, sometimes you don't get the shit mixed with the gold. I Like OWoD for it's worldbuilding, But sometimes that world-building gets weird (Killing all ravnos, Killing all russian nosfetatu, nuking the underworld) I'm apprehensive about canonizing larps (Or did I just dream that segment) because one good writer is more trustworthy than an amount of players of variable quality.<br /> I think I'd prefer a middle ground, really. A toolbox, but with a history, and maybe a step back from cataclysms and other big, sweeping changes that aren't somewhat comparable to realworld changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 10-06-2016, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T09:58:06-07:00","id":982759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982687#post982687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd prefer a middle ground, really. A toolbox, but with a history, and maybe a step back from cataclysms and other big, sweeping changes that aren't somewhat comparable to realworld changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what the CofD games are - when we say &quot;toolbox&quot; we mean &quot;you design what your city looks like in this setting unless you decide to use one of our examples&quot; and not &quot;the history of this faction is entirely undefined&quot;. <br /> <br /> Like, Mage has six Orders who all have detailed histories and are filled with members of the five Paths. Legacies have backstories; when they were invented, how they spread.<br /> <br /> The composition of [i]your[i] Consilium is up to you. That's the &quot;toolbox&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:01:47-07:00","id":982913,"title":"","content":"I'm aware that each faction has histories (well, I've only read requiem. I've heard a lot of humourous things about forksaken out of context) but I still think I need more. I like a lot of the small scale metaplot of oWoD, like the spread of anarch sorcery/the various tremere defections/assamite schism/the rise and fall of cyberdogs/the plains of the apocalypse. I've disliked and liked some of the middle sized things, like the avatar storm in mage 20 has the options of permanent or temporary, and temporary is the clear winner. <br /> <br /> I've disliked a lot of huge things. an antedulivian waking up, wrecking shit, and getting LAZOR'D doesn't actually sound too bad. But destroying everything worthwhile in the dark umbra, having modern clans become overnight bloodlines (In population, I don't mind if an Ante dies) Basically: anything that suddenly ruins characters/chronicles where they don't have the ability to react, or taking away large opportunities without suitable alternative. Those suck, and i think they're the most often ignored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:42:57-07:00","id":982966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982913#post982913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware that each faction has histories (well, I've only read requiem. I've heard a lot of humourous things about forksaken out of context) but I still think I need more.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's more. Trust me, there's more. It's not just background explaining where the different factions come from, there is an extensive and detailed history of all the supernatural creatures, their origins, the rises and falls of entire supernatural cultures and lineages, significant historical events, all intertwined with real life history. It's not a metaplot because there are no canon events or significant setting changes that occur after year 0, but that doesn't mean there isn't a story. I like to think of it like the Souls games - there is a huge amount of background and lore, but it's unobtrusive enough that you can control how much or how little that lore actually affects your play experience simply by chosing to engage or not engage with it.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the perception of Chronicles as this anemic setting with sparse history and no real depth - the same perception that leads to comments like Shane's little gem from this interview - comes from thinking that the Requiem 1e core book is indicative of the entirety of Chronicles of Darkness, and fails to recognize that the game has been around for well over a decade, building its universe that whole time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982913#post982913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like a lot of the small scale metaplot of oWoD, like the spread of anarch sorcery/the various tremere defections/assamite schism/the rise and fall of cyberdogs/the plains of the apocalypse. I've disliked and liked some of the middle sized things, like the avatar storm in mage 20 has the options of permanent or temporary, and temporary is the clear winner.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you played Chronicles, you would probably love Dark Eras. It's packed with this kind of stuff, it's just that it all happened prior to the modern era. And the modern era is a pretty narrow window, Dark Eras has things going on from the dawn of agriculture through the 1970s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=982913#post982913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've disliked a lot of huge things. an antedulivian waking up, wrecking shit, and getting LAZOR'D doesn't actually sound too bad. But destroying everything worthwhile in the dark umbra, having modern clans become overnight bloodlines (In population, I don't mind if an Ante dies) Basically: anything that suddenly ruins characters/chronicles where they don't have the ability to react, or taking away large opportunities without suitable alternative. Those suck, and i think they're the most often ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a problem in Chronicles. ChroD doesn't make it its business to make huge sweeping changes to the setting just for the sake of shaking things up or advancing the metaplot. It recognizes that individual groups are going to play out those kinds of stories at their own tables, with their own characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-06-2016, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:34:08-07:00","id":983665,"title":"","content":"Whenever Martin opens his mouth, I thank my lucky stars that he's decided CofD doesn't interest him. I reached out to new White Wolf in an email a few months back about my fears with the new direction for things and none of what I heard back gave me much hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:29:46-07:00","id":983782,"title":"","content":"Hm. I kind of personally prefer the SCP-style &quot;there is no canon&quot; approach, and there's a significant amount in the books that supports that. Ie, every one of them except Beast is written to be crossover-optional. I loved how Demon had a sidebar explaining how to run the game under the assumption that Demons only recently became free. I get that there's a &quot;default&quot;, but my favorite tack is always the multiversal &quot;this could be true&quot; approach. It's one of my favorite things about ChroD, and I like that it went to the opposite of metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T08:36:14-07:00","id":983933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=983782#post983782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I kind of personally prefer the SCP-style &amp;quot;there is no canon&amp;quot; approach, and there's a significant amount in the books that supports that. Ie, every one of them except Beast is written to be crossover-optional. I loved how Demon had a sidebar explaining how to run the game under the assumption that Demons only recently became free. I get that there's a &amp;quot;default&amp;quot;, but my favorite tack is always the multiversal &amp;quot;this could be true&amp;quot; approach. It's one of my favorite things about ChroD, and I like that it went to the opposite of metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely! One of the strong points of Chronicles is its modularity. If you want to say, &quot;Changelings don't exist in this chronicle&quot; or, &quot;in my game the Camarilla never fell&quot; or, &quot;in this story the Fall of Atlantis and the Sundering actually were the same event&quot; or what ever, you easily can. But that's also just part of the medium. You can ignore the metaplot in WoD too, or play D&amp;D in the Forgotten Realms but say Elminser and Drizt don't exist in your forgotten realms. Calling the canon of an RPG setting modular is about like calling a rule optional - it's somewhat redundant, as all RPG rules are optional, calling one out as such specifically mostly just serves to telegraph the fact that you won't break anything if you chose to ignore this particular rule. You won't break anything if you choose to ignore ChroD backstory or lore, and ChroD often helps facilitate modularity of canon by presenting &quot;what if&quot; scenarios and things like the Chronicler's Guides. Which is a great thing, playing to the medium's strengths. It's also part of the reason it doesn't work as well for transmedia as WoD does; ChroD really takes advantage of being an RPG and is really well-tailored to tabletop. WoD is a little more media-neutral, as the story could just as easily be told as a TV series, or a novel series, or a video game series, or all of the above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T10:06:46-07:00","id":983958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=983933#post983933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ChroD really takes advantage of being an RPG and is really well-tailored to tabletop. WoD is a little more media-neutral, as the story could just as easily be told as a TV series, or a novel series, or a video game series, or all of the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree with this statement, but I don't feel like this hinders ChroD in those other mediums. Did you know that Bioware chose to do SWTOR as &quot;The Old Republic&quot; because they would have more created freedom to tell the story they wanted? if they had chose to make a Clone Wars MMO, they would have had stricter rules. The point I'm making here is the same flexibility in tabletop, would also facilitate other creators creativity. They could tell whatever story they wanted so long as it was thematically within universe. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T10:15:58-07:00","id":983960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=983958#post983958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I generally agree with this statement, but I don't feel like this hinders ChroD in those other mediums. Did you know that Bioware chose to do SWTOR as &amp;quot;The Old Republic&amp;quot; because they would have more created freedom to tell the story they wanted? if they had chose to make a Clone Wars MMO, they would have had stricter rules. The point I'm making here is the same flexibility in tabletop, would also facilitate other creators creativity. They could tell whatever story they wanted so long as it was thematically within universe. </div> </div> </div> </div>Which is great from a creative perspective but challenging from a marketing perspective. There's a balance that needs to be struck between narrative freedom for the creators and narrative cohesion for the audience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T10:19:57-07:00","id":983962,"title":"","content":"I think it's less that marketing CofD would be so impossibly hard and more that marketing oWoD with the structure it has is just so relatively easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T10:45:28-07:00","id":983974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=983960#post983960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is great from a creative perspective but challenging from a marketing perspective. There's a balance that needs to be struck between narrative freedom for the creators and narrative cohesion for the audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not really sure this is hard, see star wars... (at least before disney took over and killed a large portion of the EU), actually the big challenge is to maintain an iron grip, while allowing creative freedom. As far as marketing you slap a big &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; on it, maybe a &quot;Vampire the Requiem&quot; (Se Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic, &lt;insert story title here&gt; ). I mean of course people who wanted to say they were &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; would probably have to go through some sort of approval process. I mean how do we recognize that Luke Cage is part of Marvel? and in the same universe as the Avengers movie? you know the thing with the guy with the silver hammer and the green monster. How do you allow netflix to tell a story about Harlem, and ABC (right?) to tell a story about spies? that really have nothing to do with each other, and have very different moods. What if you then released comic books that had a completely different narrative about the same characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T11:03:17-07:00","id":983979,"title":"","content":"Sure, but your examples all have consistent settings shared between the individual shows/movies/games/whatever. Which you <i>could</i> do with Chronicles of Darkness, but not without sacrificing the setting modularity we were discussing. You can establish that Luke Cage is part of the same universe as the big green guy and the guy with the silver hammer through common setting elements, but if you say that in this show, Thor was born a human and gets his power from the hammer, but in that movie, he was born in Asgard and gets his power from being a literal God, saying they're the same universe doesn't really track. If you stick with one canon setting bible for Chronicles of Darkness, you can make a transmedia franchise with it. But you can't then say &quot;in this show, only Demons exist and Vampires are made up&quot; when you've got a video game in supposedly the same universe where Vampires and Demons both exist and interact with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T11:04:48-07:00","id":983981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=983962#post983962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's less that marketing CofD would be so impossibly hard and more that marketing oWoD with the structure it has is just so relatively easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T11:33:43-07:00","id":983990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=983979#post983979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but your examples all have consistent settings shared between the individual shows/movies/games/whatever. Which you <i>could</i> do with Chronicles of Darkness, but not without sacrificing the setting modularity we were discussing. You can establish that Luke Cage is part of the same universe as the big green guy and the guy with the silver hammer through common setting elements, but if you say that in this show, Thor was born a human and gets his power from the hammer, but in that movie, he was born in Asgard and gets his power from being a literal God, saying they're the same universe doesn't really track. If you stick with one canon setting bible for Chronicles of Darkness, you can make a transmedia franchise with it. But you can't then say &amp;quot;in this show, only Demons exist and Vampires are made up&amp;quot; when you've got a video game in supposedly the same universe where Vampires and Demons both exist and interact with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div> For a CoD tv show or movie, you lean towards the default plus whatever the producers prefer.<br /> <br /> I think the key way to do a CoD TV Show/Movie is to stick closely to default, but also focus on 2e regional settings like Tokyo, Toronto, Paris, Montreal, Vancouver, LA, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T11:51:50-07:00","id":983995,"title":"","content":"I think some of that is because the WoD <b>was</b> a transmedia property before that was really what we called such things thanks to the 90s gaming boom, and the CofD has been restrained to being a TT RPG project by the gaming bust (there are some forays outside of TT, but none of have really caught on and isn't internally interactive).<br /> <br /> The WoD already had things like events in video games working into the books (Brujah Revised included the PC from the Vampire: Redemption video game as an NPC), some ARG oriented material (there was a Hunter-net.org website that had canon NPCs posting stuff as lead ins for the Time of Judgement material), and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T11:52:43-07:00","id":983996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=983990#post983990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a CoD tv show or movie, you lean towards the default plus whatever the producers prefer.<br /> <br /> I think the key way to do a CoD TV Show/Movie is to stick closely to default, but also focus on 2e regional settings like Tokyo, Toronto, Paris, Montreal, Vancouver, LA, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which you could absolutely do, but you wouldn't be taking advantage of the setting modularity. YMMV on if that's a bad thing or not, but if you're like Gecko and love the ability to create your own canon, transmedia won't give you the freedom to do that like tabletop does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T13:50:08-07:00","id":984044,"title":"","content":"I agree, the structure of WoD makes it a lot easier to market...But some pieces of what they've put <i>in</i> the structure still sounds nearly unmarketable. Vampire's a proven success (just look at Bloodlines), and Werewolf or Demon wouldn't be so difficult, but then you have Mage, which just feels so woefully esoteric that I don't know if anyone would greenlight much for it. <b>I am not saying it is bad, just hard to sell.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T14:39:38-07:00","id":984067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=983958#post983958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally agree with this statement, but I don't feel like this hinders ChroD in those other mediums.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that, once there's say, ChroD TV shows and a setting is explored, it's pretty difficult to do that while avoiding hard answers. -&quot;In my game the prince here is Whoever.&quot; -&quot;But in the TV show that's Lacroix...&quot; -&quot;But this isn't the TV show.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T14:41:15-07:00","id":984068,"title":"","content":"Fortunately, that never happened with Kindred: The Embraced. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T14:56:57-07:00","id":984071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984067#post984067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is that, once there's say, ChroD TV shows and a setting is explored, it's pretty difficult to do that while avoiding hard answers. -&quot;In my game the prince here is Whoever.&quot; -&quot;But in the TV show that's Lacroix...&quot; -&quot;But this isn't the TV show.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could perhaps try something like what Pokemon did, using multiple time lines and realities as an assumption.<br /> <br /> For instance we have 3 different continuities for the Anime, the Manga, and the Games.... which get divided even further because canonically each game <i>cartridge </i>is its own universe.... The main bridge between them is that they all superficially happen in the same world with the same creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T15:24:18-07:00","id":984081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984071#post984071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You could perhaps try something like what Pokemon did, using multiple time lines and realities as an assumption.<br /> <br /> For instance we have 3 different continuities for the Anime, the Manga, and the Games.... which get divided even further because canonically each game <i>cartridge </i>is its own universe.... The main bridge between them is that they all superficially happen in the same world with the same creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, you can make stuff work if you put your mind to it, but producers aren't known for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T16:49:47-07:00","id":984115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984067#post984067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that, once there's say, ChroD TV shows and a setting is explored, it's pretty difficult to do that while avoiding hard answers. -&quot;In my game the prince here is Whoever.&quot; -&quot;But in the TV show that's Lacroix...&quot; -&quot;But this isn't the TV show.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really easy to avoid. Sunnydale, Gotham, Riverdale, Central City, Jump City, Metropolis, the City. Fiction is full of fictional locations, even if they're just reflections of existing ones.<br /> <br /> Plus it's not as if there haven't already been set depictions of various settings that have been thrown out the window because developers pick and choose their canon.<br /> <br /> And of course, if a network figures they can make money off of a show, they are not going to care that someone is going to complain, 'But in my New York, the Prince is a Gangrel!'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984081#post984081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, you can make stuff work if you put your mind to it, but producers aren't known for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are known for hiring writers to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-08-2016, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T16:50:56-07:00","id":984116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=983979#post983979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but your examples all have consistent settings shared between the individual shows/movies/games/whatever. Which you <i>could</i> do with Chronicles of Darkness, but not without sacrificing the setting modularity we were discussing. You can establish that Luke Cage is part of the same universe as the big green guy and the guy with the silver hammer through common setting elements, but if you say that in this show, Thor was born a human and gets his power from the hammer, but in that movie, he was born in Asgard and gets his power from being a literal God, saying they're the same universe doesn't really track. If you stick with one canon setting bible for Chronicles of Darkness, you can make a transmedia franchise with it. But you can't then say &quot;in this show, only Demons exist and Vampires are made up&quot; when you've got a video game in supposedly the same universe where Vampires and Demons both exist and interact with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know. I actually feel like ChroD is basically the ideal sort of model for a transmedia property. I think that with shared universes, like the one Marvel has developed with their film and TV stable, it's more about the illusion of connectivity than the explicitness of it. I look at the properties within of the MCU as a collection of concentric circles. The Netflix shows make mention of their partner series and the events of the movies, but they're always asides. Iron Man, Thor, and Captain America have their own adventures that can largely ignore one another. It's a collection of plot points that writers and directors can pull from but aren't required to.<br /> <br /> I think the regional scale of ChroD makes it an ideal fit for that tightrope balance of a shared universe and creative license. You could have a Requiem show set in Mexico City and a Forsaken video game about a pack of werewolves embroiled in the drug wars of Oaxaca (and that's really an awesome game idea), and you never have to worry about the two bumping up against each other. And it won't affect an individual's tabletop game any more than, say, Shadows of Mexico does. If a vicious struggle between vampires and werewolves breaks out in ChroD Seattle, it's not going to greatly affect whatever stories are being told in Phoenix, or Vancouver, or Prague. But if there's a gang war between leeches and lupines in WoD Seattle, there's always that lingering question of why the Technocracy or Camarilla, or any number of other international supernatural organizations, don't get involved.<br /> <br /> I don't think ChroD is less appropriate for transmedia consumption than WoD because of its modularity. I just think the WoD is more appropriate because of its tone and style. It's more visceral and swaggering, and that makes it more appropriate to big budget aesthetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-08-2016, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T16:54:47-07:00","id":984119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984071#post984071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You could perhaps try something like what Pokemon did, using multiple time lines and realities as an assumption.<br /> <br /> For instance we have 3 different continuities for the Anime, the Manga, and the Games.... which get divided even further because canonically each game <i>cartridge </i>is its own universe.... The main bridge between them is that they all superficially happen in the same world with the same creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Using the Marvel metaphor, you have a comics continuity, a live action TV/film continuity, and any number of video games and animated shows that are in their own pocket continuities. They share characters, settings, and rough ideas, but they build out universes that play to the unique strengths of their medium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T17:16:29-07:00","id":984128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984115#post984115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's really easy to avoid. Sunnydale, Gotham, Riverdale, Central City, Jump City, Metropolis, the City. Fiction is full of fictional locations, even if they're just reflections of existing ones.<br /> <br /> Plus it's not as if there haven't already been set depictions of various settings that have been thrown out the window because developers pick and choose their canon.<br /> <br /> And of course, if a network figures they can make money off of a show, they are not going to care that someone is going to complain, 'But in my New York, the Prince is a Gangrel!'</div> </div> </div> </div>See the post above yours.<br /> <br /> And that's not even considering exploring setting defining information on a cosmic scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T17:59:58-07:00","id":984138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984067#post984067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is that, once there's say, ChroD TV shows and a setting is explored, it's pretty difficult to do that while avoiding hard answers. -&quot;In my game the prince here is Whoever.&quot; -&quot;But in the TV show that's Lacroix...&quot; -&quot;But this isn't the TV show.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>or the fact that as soon as you introduce the G-M with Splinter timelines it's a bit like DC's multiverse, or Dr Who's regeneration, where they've basically got an in game explanation for why things are different.<br /> <br /> Also, the books have defined prince's and whatever, so how do you deal with that contradiction in your game? oh right, it's baked in that you can make it whatever you want. I'm not sure how you'd do that in TV, that these are losely or perhaps not related at all stories. Maybe like American Horror Story... Just seems like something you have to explain about the setting, somehow. A narration could do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:04:01-07:00","id":984140,"title":"","content":"Actually it'd be really easy to ensure uniquess in the setting, require that anyone who wants to produce media for the setting, has to pick a location and a time period, and know that the events must be local or regional in universe impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:25:54-07:00","id":984155,"title":"","content":"We're overthinking this. Just treat video games or TV or whatnot like we treat any of the CofD fiction pieces: as a look at the world <i>as it could be</i>, from the vision of <i>a specific author</i>. A hypothetical CofD tv/movie franchise would only <i>really need</i> to be &quot;in continuity&quot; with itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:35:16-07:00","id":984162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984128#post984128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the post above yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's not even considering exploring setting defining information on a cosmic scale. </div> </div> </div>Most of the cosmic stuff is for the benefit of fans, but can simply be portrayed as is, with different groups believing they know the truth but not being able to prove it because it's cosmic, and the characters aren't. This, also, has been done loads of times in fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:02:16-07:00","id":984170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984067#post984067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is that, once there's say, ChroD TV shows and a setting is explored, it's pretty difficult to do that while avoiding hard answers. -&amp;quot;In my game the prince here is Whoever.&amp;quot; -&amp;quot;But in the TV show that's Lacroix...&amp;quot; -&amp;quot;But this isn't the TV show.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Is that any different then WoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:03:36-07:00","id":984172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984067#post984067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is that, once there's say, ChroD TV shows and a setting is explored, it's pretty difficult to do that while avoiding hard answers. -&amp;quot;In my game the prince here is Whoever.&amp;quot; -&amp;quot;But in the TV show that's Lacroix...&amp;quot; -&amp;quot;But this isn't the TV show.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Is that any different from a WoD TV show?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:03:37-07:00","id":984173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984155#post984155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're overthinking this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaaaaaaaaand thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:04:43-07:00","id":984174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=984155#post984155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're overthinking this. Just treat video games or TV or whatnot like we treat any of the CofD fiction pieces: as a look at the world <i>as it could be</i>, from the vision of <i>a specific author</i>. A hypothetical CofD tv/movie franchise would only <i>really need</i> to be &amp;quot;in continuity&amp;quot; with itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1,000,000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:49:41-07:00","id":985161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=983665#post983665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whenever Martin opens his mouth, I thank my lucky stars that he's decided CofD doesn't interest him. I reached out to new White Wolf in an email a few months back about my fears with the new direction for things and none of what I heard back gave me much hope.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Other than his attachment to the larp scene, what's he done wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:06:28-07:00","id":985172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=979214#post979214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah, he said <i>what</i> now? I'm going to have to watch the video when I get home before I draw any conclusions, but between this and his comments about how WoD should be able to address 9/11 as a metaplot point... I'm pretty sure he and I have very different views on what &quot;talking about social issues&quot; should look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as a New Yorker, I don't really want Pentex, or worse the government to be responsible for 9/11. The truth is horrific enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T00:23:57-07:00","id":985982,"title":"","content":"I don't think he means that. I thinl he means ecpliring jow those events affected the supernatural population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T03:11:21-07:00","id":986021,"title":"","content":"I'm from Poland, but plan to run ( in some future ) game about <b>Geist</b> created in 9/11 in NYC - Am I disrespectful to victims by using this event as base of chronicles on Second Chances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T06:34:38-07:00","id":986095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986021#post986021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm from Poland, but plan to run ( in some future ) game about <b>Geist</b> created in 9/11 in NYC - Am I disrespectful to victims by using this event as base of chronicles on Second Chances?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know about Second Chances, but is playing a video game set in World War II disrespectful to Jews? Or Germans for that matter? <br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think public tragic events are exempt from being converted into media, but I do believe a certain care or respect needs to be given if the event is still in recent memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-12-2016, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:43:07-07:00","id":986466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986095#post986095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know about Second Chances, but is playing a video game set in World War II disrespectful to Jews? Or Germans for that matter?<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think public tragic events are exempt from being converted into media, but I do believe a certain care or respect needs to be given if the event is still in recent memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. It's not that can't do it, it is just that if you are bending things for your story, be aware you can trample some people's nerves.<br /> <br /> Surrounding the events of 9/11? Fine.<br /> Saying the bombers were part of a (supernatural) death cult and the attack was an elaborate (supernatural) sacrifice? Problem territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:48:33-07:00","id":986470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986466#post986466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. It's not that can't do it, it is just that if you are bending things for your story, be aware you can trample some people's nerves.<br /> <br /> Surrounding the events of 9/11? Fine.<br /> Saying the bombers were part of a (supernatural) death cult and the attack was an elaborate (supernatural) sacrifice? Problem territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Even the Old WoD backed off from involving supernaturals in the Holocaust directly, and that was <i>50 years ago</i> at the time. By no means should they completely step around 9/11, because ignoring it would be ignoring a serious part of our history that informas a lot of our modern society, but it should be presented honestly, sensitively, and with respect to those who suffered and died, both in the attacks and in the subsequent conflicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T16:57:31-07:00","id":986476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986470#post986470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. Even the Old WoD backed off from involving supernaturals in the Holocaust directly, and that was <i>50 years ago</i> at the time. By no means should they completely step around 9/11, because ignoring it would be ignoring a serious part of our history that informas a lot of our modern society, but it should be presented honestly, sensitively, and with respect to those who suffered and died, both in the attacks and in the subsequent conflicts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having characters dealing with the events of 9/11, and adding a supernatural element to that (i.e. how does an event of that magnitude effect the underworld)? I think that's perfectly fine.<br /> <br /> But yeah... Attributing the attacks themselves to some supernatural force and making it a plot point is definitely a bridge too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T01:33:34-07:00","id":986633,"title":"","content":"I was thinking more only as supernatural <i>aftereffect</i> of mortals lead event. In nutshell - humans made 9/11, PCs are just Sin-Eaters that live by Geists intervention on Two Towers rumble. Still, I'm from Poland, it's to me very much separated topic. Like literally I do not known anyone who has family or friend been victim in 9/11 - still, I'm trying to build it with respect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-13-2016, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:49:25-07:00","id":986728,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, the idea of portraying 9/11 victims (remember these are real people who actually died only 15 years ago) as Sin-Eaters does rub me the wrong way. I don't know anyone who died in the attacks either, but you're still using deaths that occurred in living memory as a source for fictional characters to bring back from the dead. It wouldn't bother me as much if it was a historical game and you were playing Sin Eaters who died on the Titanic or something, but to use such a recent event as a source of the deaths of your returned characters does seem to me to trivialize the actual deaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T08:36:48-07:00","id":986781,"title":"","content":"And now you are trivializing Titanic victims as lesser than 9/11 ones - Deaths on boat are less meaningful? There should be somewhere a line where creator can just take some historical events as inspirations and try to use them.<br /> <br /> World War II setting with supernatural elements is wrong? Vietnam War? Massacre on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiananmen_Square\" target=\"_blank\">Tiananmen Square</a>? People suicided in millenial madness? War in Iraq? Who is worser starting point?<br /> <br /> To me they all are tragedies. And I sympathies with victims. Still, some good things can go from taking those events as games start points - most of them to honor events they describe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T09:30:49-07:00","id":986805,"title":"","content":"I said why I would be less bothered by it. It has passed beyond living memory and into recent history. You're free to disagree with me, I was just giving my honest opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:08:41-07:00","id":986822,"title":"","content":"People can play as whatever they want in their own games. Would I use 9/11, no, people have the right to in they're own games,freedom of speech. Or course someone saying they're insentative is also freedom of speech.<br /> <br /> Honestly its not worse then having a Supernatural cause for say homelessness, murder, domestic violence, and the myrid horrible, horrible things that happen right now to people.<br /> <br /> And one shouldn't take using those sorts of topics as an endorsement that those people actually believe that 9/11 was caused by Vampire's experimenting with a new type of blood magic say, when in the RL everybody knows it was the scum bags in Al Queda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:33:50-07:00","id":986834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986822#post986822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People can play as whatever they want in their own games. Would I use 9/11, no, people have the right to in they're own games,freedom of speech. Or course someone saying they're insentative is also freedom of speech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, despite my own distaste for it, I wouldn't try to tell anyone they couldn't do it in their own games. I wouldn't run a game that way myself, nor would I want to play in such a game, and I hope White Wolf and Onyx Path dont cover such games in official books. But what you do with your own group is your business and theirs, not mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:50:36-07:00","id":986845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986834#post986834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, despite my own distaste for it, I wouldn't try to tell anyone they couldn't do it in their own games. I wouldn't run a game that way myself, nor would I want to play in such a game, and I hope White Wolf and Onyx Path dont cover such games in official books. But what you do with your own group is your business and theirs, not mine.</div> </div> </div> </div> I doubt that they will in CoD, but I think White Wolf has said they will in OWOD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:22:18-07:00","id":986858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986845#post986845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt that they will in CoD, but I think White Wolf has said they will in OWOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's how we got on this topic. I am less than thrilled with White Wolf's stance on that, and it makes me glad they're leaving CofD alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:54:24-07:00","id":986937,"title":"","content":"In fact, if I remember correctly, Geist corebook has a Sin-Eater directly related to 9/11.<br /> <br /> And Silver Ladder book talked about the bombs in the trains in Madrid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 10-13-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:47:38-07:00","id":986962,"title":"","content":"You can talk about stuff like that, but you had better have gentle hands and sharp wits for it. This is people you're handling here.<br /> <br /> I'd dearly loved to write a New York City Freehold with the decade plus of dealing with 9/11 as a significant factor in The Hedge, but I know for a fact I couldn't do it with the above requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T15:09:04-07:00","id":986969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986962#post986962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can talk about stuff like that, but you had better have gentle hands and sharp wits for it. This is people you're handling here.<br /> <br /> I'd dearly loved to write a New York City Freehold with the decade plus of dealing with 9/11 as a significant factor in The Hedge, but I know for a fact I couldn't do it with the above requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that's something I could see happening, if it was handled carefully. In the case of Geist, it's the victims coming back from the dead part that leaves a bad taste in my mouth. But if it's how characters of [insert game line] have coped with the tragedy, that to me doesn't trivialize the deaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T16:30:33-07:00","id":987000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986937#post986937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, if I remember correctly, Geist corebook has a Sin-Eater directly related to 9/11.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it has a paragraph on ground zero and says that it's a powerful cenote (sin-eaters can draw plasm from it to power themselves), meaning there was enough death (which includes death of aspects of the city itself rather than just human life according to the paragraph) that it has become a rift between the mortal world and the underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-13-2016, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T16:32:05-07:00","id":987002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986969#post986969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, that's something I could see happening, if it was handled carefully. In the case of Geist, it's the victims coming back from the dead part that leaves a bad taste in my mouth. But if it's how characters of [insert game line] have coped with the tragedy, that to me doesn't trivialize the deaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was handled right, it'd easily be one of the best settings in Changeling. If it's not, it would be a disaster.<br /> <br /> I'm awesome, nuanced even, but gentle?<br /> <br /> I made the time between Bulwarks in a freehold about playing with the surfaces of romance nine months, for Pete's sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:20:55-07:00","id":987023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=987000#post987000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, it has a paragraph on ground zero and says that it's a powerful cenote (sin-eaters can draw plasm from it to power themselves), meaning there was enough death (which includes death of aspects of the city itself rather than just human life according to the paragraph) that it has become a rift between the mortal world and the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just looked at t, no that I'm back at home.<br /> <br /> Lea Hudson (from Hudson's Heroes krewe) as a firefighter ho died in the North Tower ad came back as a Sin-Eater.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:22:28-07:00","id":987026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986858#post986858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's how we got on this topic. I am less than thrilled with White Wolf's stance on that, and it makes me glad they're leaving CofD alone.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm happy they're leaving CoD alone for my own reasons, which have more to do with being sickened with how bean counter treated D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:26:26-07:00","id":987028,"title":"","content":"That's not a problem at all. It's not like they're suggesting he caused 9/11, which seems to me (speaking for myself) like it would be the thing I don't want them to do. Generally other New Yorkers I've seen talk about it say similar stuff.<br /> <br /> Like, Geist handled it pretty well, they just mention it had a big impact on the city's dead, and that it was a big deal for everyone, and even lead to at least one Sin-Eater. Honestly, that's actually a pretty ideal portrayal insofar as sensitivity goes.<br /> <br /> That said, Geist, for all of its messiness, has this... sincerity to it that just makes it feel really genuine when discussing it. I think it's helped by Geist not being as focused on nasty politicking as other CofD games go. So it made it an easier pill to swallow for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:57:14-07:00","id":987047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986095#post986095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know about Second Chances, but is playing a video game set in World War II disrespectful to Jews? Or Germans for that matter?<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think public tragic events are exempt from being converted into media, but I do believe a certain care or respect needs to be given if the event is still in recent memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing with products like, say Gypsies, is that it's very name is offensive. People remember it, for good reason.<br /> <br /> Now, if they released a book and named it 911: Jet-Fuel the Steel Beaming or Inside Job, you'd get the same uproar.<br /> <br /> And these guys haven't earned our trust in handling delicate subjects like the folks at OPP have. They're all bragging for things they haven't accomplished yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T19:00:27-07:00","id":987050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986781#post986781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now you are trivializing Titanic victims as lesser than 9/11 ones - Deaths on boat are less meaningful?</div> </div> </div> </div>The point being missing here is that there aren't relatives alive who could take offense to how their relative's demise is being portrayed for your, quite literal, fun and games. With 911? There are.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T19:42:11-07:00","id":987066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986021#post986021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm from Poland, but plan to run ( in some future ) game about <b>Geist</b> created in 9/11 in NYC - Am I disrespectful to victims by using this event as base of chronicles on Second Chances?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. My feelings on it are this. It is fine to tie real world atrocities in with a fictional setting if the group you play with is cool with it. As a reader, I have read fiction that uses atrocities as plot points, and i have enjoyed them.<br /> <br /> Your game idea sounds great. If you lived here, you wouldn't be able to run it with dry eyes. I was lucky not to have lost anyone personally, but I generally avoid the internet on 9/11. The day is burned into my fucking mind. I remember sitting in my first college class. The first plane hit and the teacher laughed, because planes have hit WTC before. Little planes. We thought &quot;no big deal&quot; until every first responder in the class got up one by one as their cellphones/beepers went off. I remember not being able to get in touch with my parents. They worked in Brooklyn, but we really had no idea what was going on. Was this the only target? What else was coming? I remember the funerals for weeks afterwards. Driving past processions, memorial services and the grim weight that settled on everyone. Then there are the stories that come out. My friends dad who was running late, and he saw the plane hit the building where he works. Where all his friends work. The soccer coach who went to work an hour early to make copies for his kid's youth team, and he wouldn't be there if it weren't for that. He died, making copies for his kid's soccer team. <br /> <br /> I was lucky. It still impacted me greatly. I know many people who were not lucky.<br /> <br /> The personal horror games of CofD actually really match with those emotions.<br /> <br /> In WoD, they could do a good job with it. A good example is Wraith. It dealt with the great war in a fairly elegant way, and integrated it into the metaplot of the hidden history without changing the cause.<br /> <br /> The problem is their focus on the Punk setting, and the ridiculous number of people who believe it was a &quot;inside job&quot;. I can already read the &quot;government conspiracy&quot; side bar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":2293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","user":"salientmind","date":". 10-13-2016, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T19:46:50-07:00","id":987068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986834#post986834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, despite my own distaste for it, I wouldn't try to tell anyone they couldn't do it in their own games. I wouldn't run a game that way myself, nor would I want to play in such a game, and I hope White Wolf and Onyx Path dont cover such games in official books. But what you do with your own group is your business and theirs, not mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I'm not saying people shouldn't play games involving tragedy. It could be cathartic. It could be a way of exploring bad emotions. I'm just saying that a Publishing Company should tread carefully before publishing content addressing it, especially if they are going to be using the game as a &quot;Platform.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T15:21:04-07:00","id":987461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=986728#post986728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, the idea of portraying 9/11 victims (remember these are real people who actually died only 15 years ago) as Sin-Eaters does rub me the wrong way. I don't know anyone who died in the attacks either, but you're still using deaths that occurred in living memory as a source for fictional characters to bring back from the dead. It wouldn't bother me as much if it was a historical game and you were playing Sin Eaters who died on the Titanic or something, but to use such a recent event as a source of the deaths of your returned characters does seem to me to trivialize the actual deaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>My parents lived through the 2nd world war, and we've got era's all the way through ... the 80s? so you don't think that the stuff that happened in New York, or Berlin and the way those eras are represented maybe doesn't do the same? basically I'm pointing out that there a ton of eras for which a ton of people are still alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:39:45-07:00","id":987489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=987461#post987461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My parents lived through the 2nd world war, and we've got era's all the way through ... the 80s? so you don't think that the stuff that happened in New York, or Berlin and the way those eras are represented maybe doesn't do the same? basically I'm pointing out that there a ton of eras for which a ton of people are still alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like I said, it's more the specific nature of Sin-Eaters as people who died and came back from the dead that makes it iffy for me. If you're depicting how the mass amount of death impacted the Sin-Eaters of New York that's one thing. If you're playing characters who died in the attacks and came back as Sin-Eaters, I can't honestly say I don't find that distasteful. I'd say the same of any recent tragedy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:56:27-07:00","id":987834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978952-so-the-white-wolf-q-a-from-grand-masquerade-is-up?p=987461#post987461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My parents lived through the 2nd world war, and we've got era's all the way through ... the 80s? so you don't think that the stuff that happened in New York, or Berlin and the way those eras are represented maybe doesn't do the same? basically I'm pointing out that there a ton of eras for which a ton of people are still alive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also, it is not a question of whether they deal with it. It is a question of how they deal with it. I think White Wolf handled it well when they had certain supernatural groups take part in mortal conflict, but not be the cause of mortal conflict. You can use tragedy, but don't cheapen tragedy. I'm not sure how else to phrase this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}